1
00:00:00,410 --> 00:00:03,579
Just 24 hours are given.

2
00:00:03,580 --> 00:00:06,409
The directors who will head to the third Last Stage...

3
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,079
are JEONG MIN JUN, Simeez,

4
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:09,849
BADA, and INGYOO.

5
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:13,419
The required condition for this Last Stage: 24H...

6
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:14,590
is the umbrella.

7
00:00:15,550 --> 00:00:17,159
This is crazy.

8
00:00:17,160 --> 00:00:18,220
No way.

9
00:00:19,020 --> 00:00:20,559
This is driving me crazy.

10
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:23,329
I wanted to give up at that moment.

11
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,960
(Prove yourself within 24 hours if you wish to survive.)

12
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,829
I will bloom a flower on this stage.

13
00:00:26,830 --> 00:00:28,699
I can definitely survive.

14
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:29,929
I must pour out everything I have.

15
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:31,700
Losing is not an option for me.

16
00:00:32,470 --> 00:00:34,070
I've still got it.

17
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:37,210
How was this thought of in 24 hours?

18
00:00:37,810 --> 00:00:38,910
They're determined for this.

19
00:00:39,110 --> 00:00:40,649
Won't I have the biggest advantage?

20
00:00:40,650 --> 00:00:42,309
This is my home ground.

21
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:43,849
The introduction genius!

22
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:45,949
It made me think, "Could I have thought of that?"

23
00:00:45,950 --> 00:00:48,189
That was how good the performance was.

24
00:00:48,190 --> 00:00:49,390
I really enjoyed it.

25
00:00:50,050 --> 00:00:52,719
The one to be eliminated from the third Last Stage...

26
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,290
is...

27
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:57,029
This is so tough.

28
00:00:57,030 --> 00:00:58,699
I panicked a lot.

29
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,470
It's very sad.

30
00:01:00,700 --> 00:01:04,500
(Who will survive after the third Last Stage?)

31
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,010
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

32
00:01:08,140 --> 00:01:10,680
(Last Stage: 24H)

33
00:01:15,010 --> 00:01:19,980
(Last Stage: 24H)

34
00:01:20,650 --> 00:01:24,060
Just 24 hours are given.

35
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:28,159
A competition for survival with the title of director on the line.

36
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,500
Last Stage: 24H.

37
00:01:32,430 --> 00:01:36,130
Another competition for survival will happen again today.

38
00:01:38,100 --> 00:01:41,840
This is the condition for this Last Stage: 24H.

39
00:01:41,910 --> 00:01:42,970
It's...

40
00:01:43,040 --> 00:01:44,140
the umbrella.

41
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:52,479
The umbrella is an item we are very familiar with...

42
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:55,719
made to cover us from the rain.

43
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:56,789
However,

44
00:01:56,790 --> 00:01:59,119
when umbrellas meet stage lights and video images,

45
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,129
they become a field of flowers,

46
00:02:01,130 --> 00:02:02,959
(A field of flowers)

47
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:04,829
an endless desert,

48
00:02:04,830 --> 00:02:06,730
(An endless desert)

49
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:08,429
a digital space,

50
00:02:08,430 --> 00:02:10,569
(Digital world)

51
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:12,239
and even a new world.

52
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,470
(A new world)

53
00:02:13,840 --> 00:02:16,009
They turn into an objet...

54
00:02:16,010 --> 00:02:17,840
that creates many different moments.

55
00:02:17,980 --> 00:02:19,509
Even with the same umbrellas,

56
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:22,149
the way they are interpreted and used...

57
00:02:22,150 --> 00:02:27,319
will create completely different stories and performances.

58
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:30,659
There are four directors who will be...

59
00:02:30,660 --> 00:02:32,089
in this intense competition for survival.

60
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:33,859
(Last Stage: 24H)

61
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:35,690
Skills of a top-tier player...

62
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:37,499
and outstanding directing abilities.

63
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:39,829
The complete director who is capable of everything,

64
00:02:39,830 --> 00:02:40,900
BADA.

65
00:02:41,170 --> 00:02:43,070
I can definitely survive.

66
00:02:43,130 --> 00:02:45,300
I will move to the next step right away.

67
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,239
With unique concepts...

68
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:48,940
and smart usage of props,

69
00:02:48,970 --> 00:02:51,139
this concept master...

70
00:02:51,140 --> 00:02:52,379
constantly creates new scenes.

71
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,440
Simeez.

72
00:02:54,380 --> 00:02:55,679
I must pour out everything I have.

73
00:02:55,680 --> 00:02:58,720
I have to show everyone who Simeez is.

74
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:00,119
With trendy styles...

75
00:03:00,120 --> 00:03:01,619
and tasty performances,

76
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:04,389
this director creates a bang out of nowhere.

77
00:03:04,390 --> 00:03:05,490
INGYOO.

78
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:07,330
It will be hard to beat me.

79
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:09,830
I want people to see my performance as soon as possible.

80
00:03:10,630 --> 00:03:13,869
He does his storytelling through dancing and performances.

81
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:16,299
The director who creates a work of art on stage,

82
00:03:16,300 --> 00:03:17,300
JEONG MIN JUN.

83
00:03:17,301 --> 00:03:19,399
I thought that I would definitely survive.

84
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,909
I tend to have this groundless sense of confidence...

85
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:23,039
whenever I perform during the Last Stage.

86
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:24,439
How have these four directors...

87
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:27,510
created their performances with their directing abilities?

88
00:03:27,710 --> 00:03:32,249
Now, the third Last Stage: 24H will begin.

89
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:33,350
Ready?

90
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:34,620
Fight!

91
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,919
(Last Stage: 24H)

92
00:03:37,920 --> 00:03:41,860
(Who will survive the Last Stage?)

93
00:03:43,030 --> 00:03:44,500
We're all heading out together.

94
00:03:45,160 --> 00:03:46,660
The lineup is incredible.

95
00:03:47,100 --> 00:03:48,870
This is crazy.

96
00:03:48,970 --> 00:03:53,270
We can battle each other again fair and square.

97
00:03:53,370 --> 00:03:55,640
I hoped that MIN JUN wouldn't have to go.

98
00:03:55,770 --> 00:03:57,879
It was my third time going through this.

99
00:03:57,880 --> 00:04:00,380
I can't really describe this feeling.

100
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:02,480
I feel desperate and disappointed.

101
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,420
It's devastating.

102
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:08,520
It feels like I'm always going with the wrong strategies.

103
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,520
Even during the mega mission,

104
00:04:10,560 --> 00:04:12,819
I went with a reckless plan...

105
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:15,460
even though an objet wasn't needed.

106
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,260
"I'm not a strategist."

107
00:04:17,760 --> 00:04:20,160
It feels like nothing is working out for me in this competition.

108
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:23,600
I can't imagine myself performing on stage.

109
00:04:25,300 --> 00:04:26,399
Well,

110
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:28,110
(The atmosphere is heavy in BADA's room.)

111
00:04:28,470 --> 00:04:29,669
I think I gave up...

112
00:04:29,670 --> 00:04:31,110
as soon as I saw my score.

113
00:04:33,910 --> 00:04:36,709
It made me doubt my abilities.

114
00:04:36,710 --> 00:04:39,120
As there were so many talented directors,

115
00:04:39,950 --> 00:04:42,050
I felt a limit.

116
00:04:42,450 --> 00:04:44,820
I felt ashamed of myself.

117
00:04:46,290 --> 00:04:47,759
I believe that Directors' War...

118
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:50,059
is a huge opportunity.

119
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,200
That is why...

120
00:04:51,660 --> 00:04:53,060
I wish to make the most of it.

121
00:04:53,770 --> 00:04:56,000
I don't want to leave any regrets.

122
00:04:57,270 --> 00:05:00,340
I wish for my work or dancing...

123
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:01,610
to be able to...

124
00:05:02,110 --> 00:05:04,380
move hearts once again.

125
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:07,550
I will work my socks off again to make that happen.

126
00:05:09,380 --> 00:05:12,180
The train for the elimination battle is ready to depart!

127
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:17,960
It was disappointing.

128
00:05:18,060 --> 00:05:19,089
(INGYOO: 7th)

129
00:05:19,090 --> 00:05:21,189
It was a rank I had never received before.

130
00:05:21,190 --> 00:05:23,760
It felt like a nightmare.

131
00:05:23,830 --> 00:05:25,430
Not even a silly dream would be this bad.

132
00:05:25,930 --> 00:05:27,130
But this is reality.

133
00:05:27,270 --> 00:05:29,499
I feel greatly disappointed.

134
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:31,500
I wish the ones who worked with us...

135
00:05:32,170 --> 00:05:34,509
will realize that the good moments we shared together...

136
00:05:34,510 --> 00:05:37,340
matter the most.

137
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:38,909
I'm worried...

138
00:05:38,910 --> 00:05:40,650
that this would break their heart.

139
00:05:42,510 --> 00:05:45,680
I did wish that MIN JUN wouldn't have to participate.

140
00:05:46,250 --> 00:05:47,350
(A fake laugh)

141
00:05:48,390 --> 00:05:49,390
(Screaming)

142
00:05:50,350 --> 00:05:51,789
(Flapping)

143
00:05:51,790 --> 00:05:52,960
(Punches of anger)

144
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:56,860
Gosh, it's MIN JUN's third time.

145
00:05:57,060 --> 00:05:58,160
He's going to become a master.

146
00:05:58,230 --> 00:05:59,429
This is...

147
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:00,500
tough.

148
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,169
Placing first in the team...

149
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:03,969
didn't feel that pleasant.

150
00:06:03,970 --> 00:06:05,769
The reality is that I was the head of a snake...

151
00:06:05,770 --> 00:06:06,969
that got knocked out by the tail of a dragon...

152
00:06:06,970 --> 00:06:09,139
and ended up in the Last Stage.

153
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:11,140
In total,

154
00:06:11,210 --> 00:06:13,080
I'll be working for 72 hours for every Last Stage: 24H.

155
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:16,309
Won't I have the biggest advantage in the Last Stage?

156
00:06:16,310 --> 00:06:18,520
This is my home ground.

157
00:06:18,980 --> 00:06:20,379
It's like a lineup for the final round.

158
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:21,590
(It's like a lineup for the final round.)

159
00:06:21,890 --> 00:06:24,519
I will create something to make me win.

160
00:06:24,520 --> 00:06:26,459
I'll put my soul into this.

161
00:06:26,460 --> 00:06:27,730
I must beat them all.

162
00:06:27,830 --> 00:06:30,430
The girls are going to be in tears and snot again.

163
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,999
Feeling pressure is inevitable.

164
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:33,199
I will do my best...

165
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:35,000
to burn myself up for this.

166
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,600
I will survive.

167
00:06:36,930 --> 00:06:38,039
I don't care who gets eliminated.

168
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:39,740
I will survive no matter what.

169
00:06:39,770 --> 00:06:42,440
(The choreography practice begins for the Last Stage.)

170
00:06:45,210 --> 00:06:46,939
(Screaming)

171
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:48,480
(Knocked down)

172
00:06:49,050 --> 00:06:50,450
This is crazy.

173
00:06:50,620 --> 00:06:51,719
I'm scared.

174
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,820
(Black and white umbrellas lined up in perfect order)

175
00:06:53,050 --> 00:06:54,220
Hey, umbrellas.

176
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:56,619
Are you ready?

177
00:06:56,620 --> 00:06:58,489
Have you all warmed up?

178
00:06:58,490 --> 00:07:00,119
Not yet? Let's get warmed up.

179
00:07:00,120 --> 00:07:02,160
You're still a bit stiff. Okay.

180
00:07:02,690 --> 00:07:04,430
Are you ready? Let's begin.

181
00:07:04,730 --> 00:07:07,400
(The Last Stage is this dangerous.)

182
00:07:07,730 --> 00:07:09,930
(BADA gets to her senses and checks the umbrellas first.)

183
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:12,000
I have a bad memory about umbrellas.

184
00:07:12,100 --> 00:07:13,500
It happened during "Street Woman Fighter 2."

185
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,569
During the Battle Performance,

186
00:07:16,570 --> 00:07:19,309
we had to use umbrellas.

187
00:07:19,310 --> 00:07:21,949
It felt like a routine was performed with the umbrellas in the hands.

188
00:07:21,950 --> 00:07:23,309
We weren't able to overcome...

189
00:07:23,310 --> 00:07:24,680
- the umbrella performance.
- The umbrella performance.

190
00:07:24,750 --> 00:07:27,219
I have a memory of being destroyed.

191
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:29,350
I had given up on umbrellas at that moment.

192
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:32,659
But now, I must work with umbrellas again.

193
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,260
I will use them well this time...

194
00:07:34,330 --> 00:07:36,059
and prove to everyone...

195
00:07:36,060 --> 00:07:37,629
that I have changed.

196
00:07:37,630 --> 00:07:38,630
I must overcome it.

197
00:07:38,631 --> 00:07:40,500
I can't live with that memory forever.

198
00:07:40,970 --> 00:07:42,900
I decided to think differently.

199
00:07:42,970 --> 00:07:46,199
As this could be my final performance in Directors' War,

200
00:07:46,200 --> 00:07:47,740
it will be a "happy ending."

201
00:07:48,070 --> 00:07:49,769
I will use the umbrellas for that.

202
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:51,709
Umbrellas...

203
00:07:51,710 --> 00:07:53,849
only made me feel depressed.

204
00:07:53,850 --> 00:07:57,450
I wish for the umbrellas to be filled with happy memories.

205
00:07:57,650 --> 00:07:59,649
As soon as I saw the umbrella,

206
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:02,390
I thought it looked like the petals of a flower.

207
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:05,290
I thought of ways to utilize that.

208
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:07,929
I kept thinking of ideas...

209
00:08:07,930 --> 00:08:09,790
while trying to get closer to the umbrellas.

210
00:08:10,430 --> 00:08:11,899
Like this.

211
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:12,930
(Blooming)

212
00:08:13,030 --> 00:08:14,630
It's like a flower bud, right?

213
00:08:15,130 --> 00:08:17,400
The inside part of a rose.

214
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:18,899
There must be a lot of these.

215
00:08:18,900 --> 00:08:20,610
There must be a lot on both sides.

216
00:08:20,710 --> 00:08:22,469
It's like a flower bud when they are placed together.

217
00:08:22,470 --> 00:08:25,009
They look like flower petals when they are spread out.

218
00:08:25,010 --> 00:08:28,109
I'm planning to express them as fancy bouquets.

219
00:08:28,110 --> 00:08:30,680
The beam projector will be used on the umbrellas.

220
00:08:30,980 --> 00:08:33,120
Flowers can be displayed on them.

221
00:08:33,420 --> 00:08:35,850
There's a special feature with the beam projector.

222
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:37,790
I wanted roses to be displayed.

223
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:39,559
I wanted to paint the stage with flowers.

224
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:41,860
The dancers have to use their senses when using the umbrellas.

225
00:08:42,090 --> 00:08:43,360
It can't be marked...

226
00:08:43,490 --> 00:08:45,029
like a regular choreography part.

227
00:08:45,030 --> 00:08:46,559
The details of the umbrellas...

228
00:08:46,560 --> 00:08:47,869
and the angles of the umbrellas.

229
00:08:47,870 --> 00:08:51,140
We did our best to work on those parts.

230
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:53,170
Could you focus on the angle?

231
00:08:53,270 --> 00:08:54,940
It's like this right now.

232
00:08:55,370 --> 00:08:56,510
You must hold the handle.

233
00:08:57,010 --> 00:08:58,409
(The members of Team BADA start working as one with the umbrellas.)

234
00:08:58,410 --> 00:08:59,680
There we go!

235
00:09:02,510 --> 00:09:03,710
Nice!

236
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:05,650
You look incredible!

237
00:09:06,250 --> 00:09:08,749
The concept is "Bloom."

238
00:09:08,750 --> 00:09:11,220
The concept itself gave me a lot of courage.

239
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:14,189
I am someone who will survive from the rainstorm.

240
00:09:14,190 --> 00:09:15,829
I will come back...

241
00:09:15,830 --> 00:09:18,130
and confidently secure my ticket to the semi-finals.

242
00:09:18,260 --> 00:09:19,930
Hello.

243
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:22,199
(Simeez, practice room)

244
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:24,000
Oh, gosh. Here we go again.

245
00:09:24,870 --> 00:09:26,070
How many are there?

246
00:09:26,470 --> 00:09:27,510
Is this a dream?

247
00:09:28,010 --> 00:09:30,840
The umbrellas were lined up in a scary way.

248
00:09:30,940 --> 00:09:32,480
Oh, I'm going to lose it.

249
00:09:32,980 --> 00:09:34,550
Can I do this today?

250
00:09:35,580 --> 00:09:36,680
(Sighing)

251
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:38,249
It was overwhelming at first.

252
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,750
It felt like I walked into it...

253
00:09:39,820 --> 00:09:41,620
when I wasn't ready for it.

254
00:09:41,750 --> 00:09:42,990
I'm going to lose it.

255
00:09:43,350 --> 00:09:44,820
(In despair)

256
00:09:45,390 --> 00:09:47,860
Everyone is excited, actually.

257
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,429
How will Simeez use...

258
00:09:50,430 --> 00:09:51,800
these umbrella objets?

259
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,929
I shouldn't have used objets in the first mission.

260
00:09:53,930 --> 00:09:55,400
Oh, objets...

261
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,500
Anyway, I'm confident about objets.

262
00:09:57,700 --> 00:10:01,140
I'm pretty confident about using objets.

263
00:10:01,470 --> 00:10:03,670
To list ones I've used...

264
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:07,109
Lights, cloths, various tables.

265
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:08,649
I've also used various chairs.

266
00:10:08,650 --> 00:10:10,950
Mirrors, frames, arrows.

267
00:10:11,820 --> 00:10:13,620
I'm seriously going to lose it.

268
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:17,050
I can't just do kind of well. I need to absolutely kill it...

269
00:10:17,220 --> 00:10:18,490
to keep my word.

270
00:10:18,820 --> 00:10:20,460
I'm feeling all sorts of pressure.

271
00:10:20,590 --> 00:10:23,630
I felt that I had to think of something.

272
00:10:23,690 --> 00:10:24,760
So...

273
00:10:25,230 --> 00:10:27,329
I want to be on top like this.

274
00:10:27,330 --> 00:10:29,370
But if you go on top, these things...

275
00:10:29,430 --> 00:10:31,800
But use several of these.

276
00:10:32,200 --> 00:10:33,200
- Shall we try to lift you?
- Yes.

277
00:10:33,201 --> 00:10:34,210
- One, two, three.
- One, two, three.

278
00:10:34,240 --> 00:10:35,640
- Hold on tight.
- Oh, my.

279
00:10:36,040 --> 00:10:37,210
The umbrellas...

280
00:10:37,340 --> 00:10:38,409
If not...

281
00:10:38,410 --> 00:10:39,779
(You need to be original, Simeez.)

282
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:41,410
- Oh, flip it inside out?
- Yes.

283
00:10:42,210 --> 00:10:43,449
(Slap!)

284
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:45,450
Like this. Isn't this side more comfortable?

285
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:48,690
Use 3 or 4 and put me on top.

286
00:10:48,750 --> 00:10:50,760
- Maybe consider physics?
- It won't work, right?

287
00:10:51,520 --> 00:10:53,390
- I quit.
- Should we put your feet here?

288
00:10:54,260 --> 00:10:55,790
I feel so much pressure. Objets...

289
00:10:56,630 --> 00:10:57,700
What should we do?

290
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:01,199
It's my first time at Last Stage,

291
00:11:01,200 --> 00:11:04,899
but I saw that you're more likely to win if you can create...

292
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,100
that wow factor with objets.

293
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,640
I need to make something enormous with the umbrellas.

294
00:11:09,810 --> 00:11:13,280
I'm going to slightly hang off of him like this.

295
00:11:13,610 --> 00:11:16,680
Then you'll make wings on my back.

296
00:11:16,810 --> 00:11:20,219
Fold, open, fold, open.

297
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,349
Doing that looked like wings flapping.

298
00:11:22,350 --> 00:11:24,319
I wanted it to look...

299
00:11:24,320 --> 00:11:26,319
like wings opening up...

300
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:28,430
by opening the umbrellas.

301
00:11:28,490 --> 00:11:30,660
Open, open, open, open.

302
00:11:31,500 --> 00:11:33,200
(Opening asynchronously)

303
00:11:34,100 --> 00:11:35,970
The timing will be very important.

304
00:11:36,370 --> 00:11:37,500
We're not together.

305
00:11:37,870 --> 00:11:39,700
(First, they practice to get the timing right.)

306
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:42,040
We're not together, everyone.

307
00:11:42,270 --> 00:11:44,539
The speed I wanted...

308
00:11:44,540 --> 00:11:47,109
I wanted it to be all together.

309
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:50,449
It was very hard to get the timing of opening and closing right.

310
00:11:50,450 --> 00:11:52,119
Even if we're slightly off, it's so noticeable.

311
00:11:52,120 --> 00:11:54,850
So let's keep practicing so we don't make mistakes.

312
00:11:55,090 --> 00:11:56,989
One, two, three, four.

313
00:11:56,990 --> 00:11:58,490
That was late just now. Again.

314
00:11:58,660 --> 00:12:01,759
We only had 24 hours to practice.

315
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:03,359
- We'll do it until we get it right.
- Okay.

316
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,460
We synchronized everything. Until the end.

317
00:12:06,230 --> 00:12:08,870
Seven, eight. One, two, three, four.

318
00:12:08,970 --> 00:12:10,770
There we go. Perfect.

319
00:12:11,300 --> 00:12:14,039
"Simeez is good at this sort of thing."

320
00:12:14,040 --> 00:12:15,370
I wanted to show people that.

321
00:12:15,440 --> 00:12:16,670
(Team INGYOO, practice room)

322
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:18,840
(Laughing creepily)

323
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,610
Then to the back.

324
00:12:21,110 --> 00:12:23,050
(Who are these people crowding the practice room?)

325
00:12:23,210 --> 00:12:24,580
I want to get started.

326
00:12:24,980 --> 00:12:26,280
Where are you, INGYOO?

327
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,920
Let's each take a spot and act cool.

328
00:12:29,350 --> 00:12:30,790
Where is INGYOO?

329
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:33,320
(Ta-da)

330
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,630
(The main character is here.)

331
00:12:35,660 --> 00:12:37,160
(Woo, woo, woo, woo. It loosely means "Welcome.")

332
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:39,300
Here we are. We're here.

333
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:41,270
Welcome on board, everyone.

334
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:42,899
You see these, right?

335
00:12:42,900 --> 00:12:44,270
I want to get rid of them.

336
00:12:45,570 --> 00:12:46,740
Why umbrellas?

337
00:12:46,870 --> 00:12:47,910
Let's give it a go.

338
00:12:48,270 --> 00:12:49,640
Let's just get started.

339
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,710
I didn't really have a concept.

340
00:12:51,910 --> 00:12:54,950
But for Last Stage, we needed a concept.

341
00:12:55,050 --> 00:12:56,109
The objet is priority.

342
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:59,550
I figured the outcome will really depend on how we use it.

343
00:12:59,920 --> 00:13:01,489
So we used the umbrellas in various ways.

344
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,420
We flipped them, made stabbing motions.

345
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:06,760
Even if it's a bit childish, I wanted it to have impact.

346
00:13:06,860 --> 00:13:08,490
Or maybe play up the mood of the song...

347
00:13:08,690 --> 00:13:11,260
and use it like a tail, like an animal.

348
00:13:11,300 --> 00:13:13,229
(Bobbing his head)

349
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:15,630
(Loving it)

350
00:13:15,800 --> 00:13:17,100
That's hilarious.

351
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:19,170
Kind of "Madagascar" vibes.

352
00:13:19,670 --> 00:13:21,070
Hold on.

353
00:13:21,210 --> 00:13:23,040
I'm not confident about making it animal-themed.

354
00:13:23,110 --> 00:13:24,210
Let's try it as people.

355
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:26,280
How should the opening be?

356
00:13:26,410 --> 00:13:29,649
We need to show the concept in the intro.

357
00:13:29,650 --> 00:13:31,950
So I thought very carefully about the opening.

358
00:13:32,020 --> 00:13:33,020
What should we do?

359
00:13:33,021 --> 00:13:35,150
If we're using props, we have to do something with them.

360
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:37,449
Try placing them like a ladder.

361
00:13:37,450 --> 00:13:39,189
We were thinking of making a bridge sort of thing...

362
00:13:39,190 --> 00:13:40,690
and crossing it.

363
00:13:40,820 --> 00:13:41,830
It's weird.

364
00:13:41,890 --> 00:13:42,930
Pass!

365
00:13:43,090 --> 00:13:44,090
Pass.

366
00:13:44,830 --> 00:13:47,230
The story isn't flowing.

367
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:48,670
So I was thinking about it.

368
00:13:48,770 --> 00:13:50,299
Are you an umbrella seller? Wholesale?

369
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:52,070
Six, seven, eight.

370
00:13:52,600 --> 00:13:55,210
Let's give out umbrellas one by one, like a factory.

371
00:13:55,310 --> 00:13:57,109
Go, go, go. It's fun.

372
00:13:57,110 --> 00:13:58,380
Ours is the most fun.

373
00:13:58,810 --> 00:14:00,779
We got in a circle. And three.

374
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:02,480
And four. And five.

375
00:14:02,910 --> 00:14:04,520
Nice. Very nice.

376
00:14:04,820 --> 00:14:06,650
So we made an impactful intro.

377
00:14:07,250 --> 00:14:10,650
Then suddenly, the umbrellas looked like swords.

378
00:14:10,920 --> 00:14:11,920
Distribute swords...

379
00:14:11,921 --> 00:14:13,820
Distribute swords and go on a mission?

380
00:14:14,260 --> 00:14:15,860
That's visually nice too.

381
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,100
Should we be ninjas?

382
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,360
That's amazing.

383
00:14:19,460 --> 00:14:20,700
(Going right into character)

384
00:14:20,860 --> 00:14:22,670
That's new. No one has done this.

385
00:14:22,870 --> 00:14:25,100
Using umbrellas as ninjas...

386
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:27,140
There's something here. I think we can do something.

387
00:14:27,240 --> 00:14:29,810
Like ninjas that use sorcery.

388
00:14:29,970 --> 00:14:31,510
You think they're swords, but suddenly,

389
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:33,940
they turn out to be umbrellas. That kind of thing.

390
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:36,280
We're on a mission, but then we start to fly.

391
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:40,020
We created a character that can have fun,

392
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:41,720
even while on a mission.

393
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,320
What I'm sure of is that it'll be fun.

394
00:14:44,420 --> 00:14:47,459
If we mix Asian culture and my otaku-ness,

395
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,830
that'll create synergy.

396
00:14:48,890 --> 00:14:51,129
I've been doing things last minute all my life.

397
00:14:51,130 --> 00:14:53,999
This time, swordsmanship came to me at the last minute.

398
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,300
(Team JEONG MIN JUN, practice room)

399
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,129
Objet.

400
00:14:57,130 --> 00:14:59,940
(JEONG MIN JUN dives into studying the objet.)

401
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:01,540
Out of all props we had so far,

402
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:03,039
this is number one.

403
00:15:03,040 --> 00:15:04,680
It's the hardest to use.

404
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:06,639
I want to break all of the umbrellas.

405
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:08,249
The table and cube were on the easy side.

406
00:15:08,250 --> 00:15:10,409
Before, we could go on top of the props,

407
00:15:10,410 --> 00:15:12,119
use them flipped over,

408
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,080
or use them as a backdrop.

409
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:15,519
But umbrellas...

410
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:18,120
have to be carried.

411
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,759
I thought we would lose points...

412
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:23,029
if we were carrying umbrellas and suddenly put them down to dance.

413
00:15:23,030 --> 00:15:25,460
So the key for me was to use the umbrellas...

414
00:15:25,500 --> 00:15:27,900
in a way that fit the story the best.

415
00:15:28,170 --> 00:15:30,929
It can't just be creative. It needs to go with the story.

416
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,599
In "Last Stage," meaning is important.

417
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:34,510
Why did we use this prop this way?

418
00:15:34,640 --> 00:15:36,540
Why did it have to be presented like this?

419
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,240
How convincing that is is the key.

420
00:15:38,410 --> 00:15:41,580
Also, it's very important to use it in a unique way.

421
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:43,580
How can we create a dramatic effect?

422
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:44,780
Umbrellas...

423
00:15:44,781 --> 00:15:46,549
How can I take this odd and difficult ingredient...

424
00:15:46,550 --> 00:15:49,350
and cook it into something delicious?

425
00:15:51,160 --> 00:15:52,860
I thought of weapons.

426
00:15:52,960 --> 00:15:54,829
When guys are holding umbrellas,

427
00:15:54,830 --> 00:15:56,760
we always have sword fights.

428
00:15:57,030 --> 00:15:58,459
Hit the middle.

429
00:15:58,460 --> 00:15:59,830
So you have to hold the end.

430
00:15:59,930 --> 00:16:01,170
Like this. Sword fight.

431
00:16:01,300 --> 00:16:03,329
I thought of war-related concepts.

432
00:16:03,330 --> 00:16:04,769
I want to create a display...

433
00:16:04,770 --> 00:16:06,239
of people in ancient history...

434
00:16:06,240 --> 00:16:08,910
moving about at night before they head off to war.

435
00:16:09,410 --> 00:16:11,740
Hit, then pull with them connected.

436
00:16:12,040 --> 00:16:13,810
We tried using the hook of the umbrellas...

437
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:16,710
to make connections.

438
00:16:16,810 --> 00:16:18,880
We tried jumping like long-armed monkeys.

439
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:20,350
Can you try making a bunker?

440
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:23,750
We tried creating various images.

441
00:16:23,890 --> 00:16:25,390
But... I don't see a mood.

442
00:16:25,760 --> 00:16:28,560
Our movements don't have a mood that connects to war.

443
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:30,260
Oh, no. It's too abstract.

444
00:16:30,490 --> 00:16:33,500
Thinking about it as war is making it more difficult.

445
00:16:33,730 --> 00:16:36,730
We did some ideation to broaden our minds.

446
00:16:36,830 --> 00:16:39,570
I like the idea of flipping things inside out.

447
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:41,040
(Oh, my!)

448
00:16:41,210 --> 00:16:42,670
- Oh, my.
- It worked.

449
00:16:43,570 --> 00:16:45,280
(He successfully flipped the umbrella.)

450
00:16:45,340 --> 00:16:46,440
(An unexpected discovery)

451
00:16:46,740 --> 00:16:48,879
- Oh, that's cool.
- The last idea I had...

452
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:50,110
was to flip them inside out.

453
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:51,620
Then we happened to have a light.

454
00:16:51,650 --> 00:16:53,380
The light reflects off of them.

455
00:16:53,720 --> 00:16:54,950
It's like a torch.

456
00:16:55,090 --> 00:16:58,289
Torches also have a fire in basket-like things.

457
00:16:58,290 --> 00:17:01,329
I thought it would be appropriate to depict torches.

458
00:17:01,330 --> 00:17:03,759
As someone who's been on Last Stage three times,

459
00:17:03,760 --> 00:17:06,259
I thought my use of objets...

460
00:17:06,260 --> 00:17:07,400
has been very good.

461
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:09,499
I'm going to survive this Last Stage no matter what.

462
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,440
(Last Stage D-Day)

463
00:17:11,700 --> 00:17:14,040
- Hello.
- Hello.

464
00:17:14,570 --> 00:17:16,510
- Hello.
- Hello.

465
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:18,480
They're displaying roses.

466
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:21,280
What is their concept? "The Rose of Versailles?"

467
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:24,109
Adjust the umbrella angle a bit, Yu Rim.

468
00:17:24,110 --> 00:17:25,450
It's pretty. It's like a flower.

469
00:17:25,550 --> 00:17:26,750
It looks like a flower bud.

470
00:17:26,850 --> 00:17:28,249
To the audience,

471
00:17:28,250 --> 00:17:29,689
it looks like an art wall.

472
00:17:29,690 --> 00:17:33,020
It creates an impact before you get started.

473
00:17:33,120 --> 00:17:35,289
Keep it like that,

474
00:17:35,290 --> 00:17:37,190
and we'll do the beam projector.

475
00:17:37,760 --> 00:17:39,960
Oh, they're lining each one up with a flower.

476
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:42,769
The numbering is very important here...

477
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:45,269
because they're projecting a flower...

478
00:17:45,270 --> 00:17:47,200
on each one of your umbrellas.

479
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:50,139
So if we get this wrong, it'll all be off.

480
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:51,580
(Nervous)

481
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:54,980
I can see why BEBE is always so synchronized.

482
00:17:55,450 --> 00:17:56,510
You're not in the right square.

483
00:17:56,650 --> 00:17:58,850
(A dancer is not in line?)

484
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:01,520
(I think I'm in line...)

485
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:04,960
Ga Eun's row has to move 0.000001cm over.

486
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,590
How can you move 0.000001cm?

487
00:18:08,090 --> 00:18:09,429
The slightest bit...

488
00:18:09,430 --> 00:18:11,030
Do you just have to imagine moving?

489
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:12,460
(Glancing over)

490
00:18:12,700 --> 00:18:14,329
They just did. I saw it.

491
00:18:14,330 --> 00:18:15,800
- They just did?
- Yes.

492
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:17,600
You have to almost not move.

493
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:21,039
- Please remember that spot.
- Can you move back a bit?

494
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,270
Ready. Go.

495
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:24,510
One, two, three, four.

496
00:18:24,710 --> 00:18:26,740
Five, six. Don't get too excited.

497
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,950
One, two, three, four.

498
00:18:29,110 --> 00:18:30,650
(The umbrella didn't close.)

499
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:33,020
Five and six. Again.

500
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:34,220
Sorry.

501
00:18:34,690 --> 00:18:35,820
(Feeling bad)

502
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:38,120
I'm so sorry, but I can't let things slip anymore.

503
00:18:38,220 --> 00:18:39,720
(Things suddenly get tense.)

504
00:18:39,890 --> 00:18:41,430
I need you to wake up.

505
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:42,589
- Okay.
- Okay.

506
00:18:42,590 --> 00:18:44,059
I think that was the most on edge I've been...

507
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:45,600
during all of Directors' War.

508
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:47,759
We got everything in sync in the practice room...

509
00:18:47,760 --> 00:18:49,070
and came on set.

510
00:18:49,330 --> 00:18:50,930
But everything fell apart.

511
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,840
Everyone was out of place and all.

512
00:18:53,940 --> 00:18:55,069
I didn't know what to do.

513
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:57,110
Because if we don't do well, we have to go home.

514
00:18:57,170 --> 00:18:59,279
If we don't get the details right for each and every person,

515
00:18:59,280 --> 00:19:00,339
we'll definitely be eliminated.

516
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,910
I was worried they'd stop focusing,

517
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:05,450
so I needed to say something strong.

518
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:08,490
Get into formation and mark your numbers.

519
00:19:08,650 --> 00:19:10,649
I'll give you five seconds to get into formation.

520
00:19:10,650 --> 00:19:14,020
Five, four, three,

521
00:19:14,730 --> 00:19:17,229
- two, one.
- Oh, my gosh.

522
00:19:17,230 --> 00:19:18,299
(They got into formation in just 5 seconds.)

523
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:19,930
I think we got it. You can come down now.

524
00:19:20,230 --> 00:19:23,130
After seeing them research some of these parts,

525
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,440
- I'm very excited.
- I think it'll look good.

526
00:19:25,700 --> 00:19:27,470
Should we check the beam projector first?

527
00:19:27,570 --> 00:19:29,410
(Checking the projection part at the start of rehearsal)

528
00:19:29,810 --> 00:19:31,240
The projector is very big.

529
00:19:31,740 --> 00:19:34,480
I think Simeez will be good at creating big pictures.

530
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:37,050
She has always liked using objets.

531
00:19:37,280 --> 00:19:40,079
Hee Jung is good at using objets.

532
00:19:40,080 --> 00:19:41,750
I was very excited about that.

533
00:19:42,150 --> 00:19:44,860
Lights and special effects are very important.

534
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,160
So we checked those first.

535
00:19:46,320 --> 00:19:47,389
(Checking the next projection)

536
00:19:47,390 --> 00:19:48,930
(Shaking her head)

537
00:19:49,390 --> 00:19:50,760
It's not visible right now.

538
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,460
It's too faint.

539
00:19:52,860 --> 00:19:54,400
- It's too hard to see.
- This is the part.

540
00:19:54,900 --> 00:19:56,100
(Wondering what to do)

541
00:19:56,300 --> 00:19:58,339
When it comes to beam projectors,

542
00:19:58,340 --> 00:20:00,300
you really need to control the lights well.

543
00:20:00,340 --> 00:20:02,009
You really have to choose what to focus on.

544
00:20:02,010 --> 00:20:03,410
And you always have to have a blackout.

545
00:20:03,540 --> 00:20:05,540
The projection wasn't really visible.

546
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:08,550
I thought it'd be easier to see without the lights.

547
00:20:08,650 --> 00:20:11,480
I want all the lights off for this part as well.

548
00:20:11,850 --> 00:20:13,149
(Boldly turning the lights off)

549
00:20:13,150 --> 00:20:15,819
- Good job.
- When we're using the projector,

550
00:20:15,820 --> 00:20:18,690
we need to put the focus on the performance.

551
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:21,630
Those are hands. I think they're using hands.

552
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:24,130
I'm so curious what the concept is.

553
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:26,760
The choreography, the objet, the projection,

554
00:20:26,900 --> 00:20:28,770
and the concept I chose.

555
00:20:28,900 --> 00:20:32,600
I think it was most important to bring those things together.

556
00:20:32,800 --> 00:20:37,170
Let's run it through with Simeez.

557
00:20:37,470 --> 00:20:38,879
(They start to run through the performance.)

558
00:20:38,880 --> 00:20:39,980
Are you ready? One, two.

559
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:42,979
She got on his back.

560
00:20:42,980 --> 00:20:44,849
I think there's some sort of story.

561
00:20:44,850 --> 00:20:47,480
Is she going somewhere?

562
00:20:47,620 --> 00:20:50,219
"Simeez is good at this sort of thing."

563
00:20:50,220 --> 00:20:51,519
I wanted to show people that.

564
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:52,920
I'll definitely come back.

565
00:20:53,260 --> 00:20:54,319
That's cool.

566
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:55,330
(Getting into it)

567
00:20:55,930 --> 00:20:56,930
(Oh, my.)

568
00:20:56,930 --> 00:20:57,930
Nice.

569
00:20:57,931 --> 00:21:00,430
Now what will INGYOO use?

570
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,799
Should we try running it?

571
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:02,900
- Okay.
- Okay.

572
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:04,699
Ninja?

573
00:21:04,700 --> 00:21:06,440
Yes, like a ninja.

574
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:09,339
INGYOO never does cliche things.

575
00:21:09,340 --> 00:21:10,809
So I'm very excited.

576
00:21:10,810 --> 00:21:12,380
Is all of WE DEM BOYZ here?

577
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,350
Stretch your hamstrings. Hinge at the hips.

578
00:21:16,650 --> 00:21:18,049
Your head should touch the floor.

579
00:21:18,050 --> 00:21:19,220
You need to loosen up more.

580
00:21:19,320 --> 00:21:20,679
I pushed them...

581
00:21:20,680 --> 00:21:23,250
to get into their best physical conditions.

582
00:21:23,390 --> 00:21:24,659
- The part with the spotlight.
- Yes?

583
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:26,689
Can you turn off all lights except the spotlight?

584
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:28,060
Please turn off the front light.

585
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:30,029
- This is good.
- Like this.

586
00:21:30,030 --> 00:21:31,430
We'll go with this mood.

587
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:34,400
I had to intensely check everything, lights and all.

588
00:21:34,500 --> 00:21:37,029
Do the ninja running pose.

589
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:38,199
That part.

590
00:21:38,200 --> 00:21:39,640
(Practicing the choreography)

591
00:21:40,140 --> 00:21:41,200
Again.

592
00:21:41,300 --> 00:21:42,569
Seven and eight.

593
00:21:42,570 --> 00:21:44,070
Again. Let's do it again.

594
00:21:44,610 --> 00:21:45,710
Again.

595
00:21:45,810 --> 00:21:46,810
Oh, my.

596
00:21:46,811 --> 00:21:48,510
I can feel the tension.

597
00:21:48,850 --> 00:21:49,979
It's like this.

598
00:21:49,980 --> 00:21:51,279
(INGYOO demonstrates the move.)

599
00:21:51,280 --> 00:21:53,050
I want it to be more like this. Do you get what I mean?

600
00:21:53,150 --> 00:21:55,649
(Ting! Bralalala)

601
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:57,220
I want it to go like this, but right now...

602
00:21:57,420 --> 00:21:58,689
(Dum, dan, dda)

603
00:21:58,690 --> 00:21:59,919
This. No.

604
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:00,920
- Okay.
- Okay!

605
00:22:00,921 --> 00:22:02,190
Slide. Again. Five.

606
00:22:02,490 --> 00:22:04,700
Details to make us look like ninjas.

607
00:22:04,900 --> 00:22:07,300
We created a good performance, so I wanted to do very well.

608
00:22:07,430 --> 00:22:09,100
The concept is clear,

609
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:10,569
but I'm curious how it'll turn out.

610
00:22:10,570 --> 00:22:12,740
We need one big bang.

611
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:15,240
You need people to go, "Oh, my!" to survive.

612
00:22:15,340 --> 00:22:16,540
I was that confident.

613
00:22:16,910 --> 00:22:18,780
INGYOO's mindset is really like,

614
00:22:19,080 --> 00:22:20,210
"I will not lose."

615
00:22:20,410 --> 00:22:23,250
He's determined to survive.

616
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:25,720
Hello.

617
00:22:26,050 --> 00:22:27,479
We are always here.

618
00:22:27,480 --> 00:22:29,350
Are The Stories here?

619
00:22:29,450 --> 00:22:31,090
I think MIN JUN's will be fun.

620
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:34,289
MIN JUN has the power to make people look forward to his performance.

621
00:22:34,290 --> 00:22:35,290
Yes.

622
00:22:35,291 --> 00:22:38,859
I tried to line up the lights...

623
00:22:38,860 --> 00:22:41,430
to the tone and timing of the performance.

624
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:42,700
Can you open it?

625
00:22:42,930 --> 00:22:44,370
(Whipping open)

626
00:22:44,630 --> 00:22:45,940
(Skillful)

627
00:22:46,170 --> 00:22:47,500
It's like a torch.

628
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:50,610
Insane. That's an amazing idea.

629
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:52,580
(Satisfied)

630
00:22:52,910 --> 00:22:54,809
The projection was good, the lights were good,

631
00:22:54,810 --> 00:22:56,450
the choreography was good, and the formations were good.

632
00:22:57,080 --> 00:22:58,150
What could it be?

633
00:22:58,280 --> 00:23:00,650
The synopsis is intriguing, so I'm also curious about the costumes.

634
00:23:01,020 --> 00:23:03,090
I felt our performance would be very cool.

635
00:23:03,390 --> 00:23:05,320
I'm going to survive this Last Stage no matter what.

636
00:23:05,920 --> 00:23:08,059
The biggest merit...

637
00:23:08,060 --> 00:23:09,829
is that it's the third episode of Last Stage.

638
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:12,600
I think I'll be one of the two that survive.

639
00:23:12,760 --> 00:23:13,999
We'll create an amazing performance...

640
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,569
that no one has ever seen before.

641
00:23:16,570 --> 00:23:18,469
I'll push myself to the extreme...

642
00:23:18,470 --> 00:23:21,200
and produce the best performance in my own style.

643
00:23:21,510 --> 00:23:22,709
I want to dance soon.

644
00:23:22,710 --> 00:23:24,470
I want people to see this soon.

645
00:23:24,610 --> 00:23:26,610
Someone better than me? I don't think there is anyone.

646
00:23:29,650 --> 00:23:31,010
(Last Stage: 24H)

647
00:23:31,820 --> 00:23:33,619
(Last Stage: 24H)

648
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:34,819
The Directors' War of Choreographers,

649
00:23:34,820 --> 00:23:37,620
where we go beyond performance and create works of art.

650
00:23:37,750 --> 00:23:40,420
Out of the four choreographers standing at the edge of the cliff,

651
00:23:40,490 --> 00:23:43,630
who will be the two who protect their names to the end?

652
00:23:43,790 --> 00:23:45,699
This competition was made for me.

653
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:47,899
The girls will be all tears.

654
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:49,970
It'll be fun. It'll be very intense.

655
00:23:50,070 --> 00:23:51,129
Please bring the right attitude...

656
00:23:51,130 --> 00:23:52,639
- as we walk in.
- Okay.

657
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,369
- I'm a rose.
- Okay.

658
00:23:54,370 --> 00:23:55,410
Okay.

659
00:23:55,970 --> 00:23:58,440
We will now introduce the Fight Judges...

660
00:23:58,580 --> 00:24:00,709
who will decide their fate.

661
00:24:00,710 --> 00:24:04,010
(Excited)

662
00:24:04,180 --> 00:24:05,950
The lineup of judges is actually the most important.

663
00:24:06,120 --> 00:24:08,320
I'm most curious about the Fight Judges.

664
00:24:08,850 --> 00:24:10,750
That wasn't that important to us.

665
00:24:11,420 --> 00:24:14,189
A director who displays endless new possibilities...

666
00:24:14,190 --> 00:24:18,060
with their out-of-the-box perspective.

667
00:24:18,400 --> 00:24:19,400
Monika!

668
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:22,769
(Monika)

669
00:24:22,770 --> 00:24:24,600
(Happy)

670
00:24:25,670 --> 00:24:27,440
It's Monika.

671
00:24:27,570 --> 00:24:28,570
Hello.

672
00:24:29,310 --> 00:24:30,410
I'm so happy to see her now.

673
00:24:31,610 --> 00:24:34,340
A choreographer who has created perfect performances.

674
00:24:34,540 --> 00:24:37,710
A performance director who shines on stage and as an artist.

675
00:24:38,080 --> 00:24:39,120
Shim Jae Won.

676
00:24:42,450 --> 00:24:44,549
Next, a choreographer who captured the world's attention...

677
00:24:44,550 --> 00:24:46,990
with their creative concepts and performances...

678
00:24:47,190 --> 00:24:49,429
that no one else can replicate.

679
00:24:49,430 --> 00:24:52,500
(Who?)

680
00:24:52,830 --> 00:24:55,770
The creator and director who leads Avantgardey.

681
00:24:55,970 --> 00:24:57,000
Akane.

682
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:00,170
Oh, is that Akane?

683
00:25:01,910 --> 00:25:03,140
(Akane)

684
00:25:04,640 --> 00:25:06,040
Oh, yes.

685
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:08,709
(The bubbly dance took over Japan in 2017.)

686
00:25:08,710 --> 00:25:10,610
Japanese high school girl concept?

687
00:25:10,710 --> 00:25:14,049
It's a dance team that wears all the same wigs...

688
00:25:14,050 --> 00:25:16,390
and Japanese school uniforms and is very synchronized.

689
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:18,320
They put on performances...

690
00:25:18,560 --> 00:25:21,390
that really capture the audience's attention.

691
00:25:21,890 --> 00:25:23,659
(Director Akane perfects her performances...)

692
00:25:23,660 --> 00:25:24,899
(with creative ideas and stage production.)

693
00:25:24,900 --> 00:25:26,760
I wonder what sort of style Akane likes.

694
00:25:27,100 --> 00:25:28,200
I was confident.

695
00:25:28,430 --> 00:25:29,730
To entertain them.

696
00:25:30,170 --> 00:25:31,500
Half excited and half nervous?

697
00:25:31,600 --> 00:25:33,800
Because we got the best reaction during the run-through.

698
00:25:33,940 --> 00:25:36,240
For this Last Stage: 24H,

699
00:25:36,440 --> 00:25:38,840
all four choreographers started...

700
00:25:39,680 --> 00:25:41,580
with the same amount of time and same conditions.

701
00:25:41,850 --> 00:25:44,380
What makes the difference in their performances...

702
00:25:44,550 --> 00:25:46,579
will be the perspective and interpretation...

703
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:48,290
each director brings to the given conditions.

704
00:25:48,490 --> 00:25:49,950
Fight Judge Shim Jae Won,

705
00:25:50,050 --> 00:25:52,220
what standards will you use to judge the performances today?

706
00:25:52,590 --> 00:25:54,960
The intention of the director,

707
00:25:55,090 --> 00:25:57,759
level of perfection, and expression.

708
00:25:57,760 --> 00:26:00,800
I'll do my best to look at those in a balanced way.

709
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:02,769
There was a limited amount of time...

710
00:26:02,770 --> 00:26:05,839
and an objet they had to use.

711
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:07,940
I imagine they must've had to utilize their experiences...

712
00:26:08,040 --> 00:26:11,469
and backgrounds to think on their feet.

713
00:26:11,470 --> 00:26:13,409
So I'll choose the director...

714
00:26:13,410 --> 00:26:15,409
who has the best balance of all of those things...

715
00:26:15,410 --> 00:26:18,619
and really does well.

716
00:26:18,620 --> 00:26:20,050
She's so sharp that it almost feels cold.

717
00:26:20,250 --> 00:26:22,289
(BADA, get it together.)

718
00:26:22,290 --> 00:26:25,690
I highly value uniqueness.

719
00:26:25,990 --> 00:26:28,430
And I also want to look at how the music and production...

720
00:26:28,490 --> 00:26:32,629
are displayed together with the same sense of direction...

721
00:26:32,630 --> 00:26:36,400
rather than those things going about on their own.

722
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:38,230
(Full of excitement)

723
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:40,639
What is clear is that it's hard for me to lose.

724
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,509
I'll definitely survive.

725
00:26:42,510 --> 00:26:44,270
I'll come back alive once again.

726
00:26:44,540 --> 00:26:45,810
I'll give it my all. Let's go.

727
00:26:45,910 --> 00:26:47,609
Before the performances,

728
00:26:47,610 --> 00:26:50,079
we have a special guest...

729
00:26:50,080 --> 00:26:52,180
at Last Stage: 24H today.

730
00:26:52,350 --> 00:26:53,819
The lead of the popular Netflix series,

731
00:26:53,820 --> 00:26:56,150
"To All the Boys I've Loved Before..."

732
00:26:56,390 --> 00:26:57,420
Hold on.

733
00:26:58,220 --> 00:27:01,490
I'm not exaggerating. That's my favorite Netflix series.

734
00:27:01,690 --> 00:27:03,430
And the action film...

735
00:27:03,660 --> 00:27:05,700
that'll premiere this coming October,

736
00:27:06,130 --> 00:27:07,630
"Street Fighter."

737
00:27:08,160 --> 00:27:11,200
(Source: Lotte Entertainment)

738
00:27:11,970 --> 00:27:14,400
It's Noah Centineo. Welcome.

739
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:16,970
(Fascinated)

740
00:27:18,680 --> 00:27:19,680
Hello.

741
00:27:20,040 --> 00:27:21,110
- Hello!
- Hello!

742
00:27:21,810 --> 00:27:22,810
He's cute.

743
00:27:22,811 --> 00:27:25,849
I heard there was this incredible dance competition show called...

744
00:27:25,850 --> 00:27:27,480
"Street World Fighter."

745
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:29,449
The directors and dancers have...

746
00:27:29,450 --> 00:27:32,389
incredible performances prepared for you.

747
00:27:32,390 --> 00:27:35,030
I am so excited, and I cannot wait for you to see it.

748
00:27:35,390 --> 00:27:37,490
(Us too)

749
00:27:37,730 --> 00:27:39,660
Now, the choreographers...

750
00:27:39,760 --> 00:27:41,769
to prove themselves with their names and creations.

751
00:27:41,770 --> 00:27:44,499
The performances that'll determine their fates will begin now.

752
00:27:44,500 --> 00:27:45,799
Which two directors...

753
00:27:45,800 --> 00:27:48,510
will protect their name with just one performance?

754
00:27:49,470 --> 00:27:52,580
Last Stage: 24H starts now.

755
00:27:52,710 --> 00:27:54,539
Are you ready?

756
00:27:54,540 --> 00:27:56,550
Fight!

757
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:59,850
The first director to start off Last Stage...

758
00:28:00,350 --> 00:28:01,380
is BADA.

759
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:03,450
(It's BADA right off the bat!)

760
00:28:04,420 --> 00:28:05,820
She must be nervous.

761
00:28:05,990 --> 00:28:08,490
BADA created something so new and cool.

762
00:28:08,730 --> 00:28:10,090
We finally get to see it.

763
00:28:10,760 --> 00:28:12,500
Is their concept "The Rose of Versailles?"

764
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:14,660
I guess BADA is a princess after all.

765
00:28:14,800 --> 00:28:16,070
Oh, so pretty.

766
00:28:16,270 --> 00:28:17,370
White Rose is here.

767
00:28:17,500 --> 00:28:18,500
(Bursting into laughter)

768
00:28:18,501 --> 00:28:20,100
(I've never seen her like this.)

769
00:28:20,370 --> 00:28:22,210
It's so funny to see her wearing a dress.

770
00:28:22,610 --> 00:28:23,639
Oh, really?

771
00:28:23,640 --> 00:28:24,940
(Spinning around doing princess bows)

772
00:28:25,380 --> 00:28:26,580
I've never seen her like that.

773
00:28:27,040 --> 00:28:29,809
Actually, it's a concept I've really wanted to do.

774
00:28:29,810 --> 00:28:30,880
I really wanted to,

775
00:28:31,010 --> 00:28:33,779
but cool, girl-crush concepts suit me well,

776
00:28:33,780 --> 00:28:37,049
so I kept pushing this off.

777
00:28:37,050 --> 00:28:39,960
But I thought of this as my last-ever chance and gave it a shot.

778
00:28:40,320 --> 00:28:44,590
The concept of my Last Stage is "Bloom."

779
00:28:44,690 --> 00:28:47,599
I chose the concept, "Bloom."

780
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:49,029
(During the first practice session, Gently flapping)

781
00:28:49,030 --> 00:28:50,130
It's kind of like a flower.

782
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:51,570
I need a flower.

783
00:28:51,800 --> 00:28:55,640
As soon as I saw the umbrellas, flowers came to mind.

784
00:28:55,740 --> 00:28:57,669
Just because I went to Last Stage,

785
00:28:57,670 --> 00:28:59,239
it doesn't mean I've wilted.

786
00:28:59,240 --> 00:29:01,979
I have grown, and I can bloom once again.

787
00:29:01,980 --> 00:29:04,380
This must be good to use in the performance.

788
00:29:04,610 --> 00:29:06,580
Make a circle formation.

789
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:11,190
I think the kick is to create a huge flower bud.

790
00:29:11,690 --> 00:29:13,890
Flower bud coming in. Excuse me.

791
00:29:14,290 --> 00:29:15,330
Thank you.

792
00:29:15,430 --> 00:29:18,330
I wanted it to look like flower petals blooming.

793
00:29:19,130 --> 00:29:21,929
And the fact that I'm inside of it is the kick.

794
00:29:21,930 --> 00:29:24,699
I, someone who doesn't seem to belong in there,

795
00:29:24,700 --> 00:29:25,840
pops out?

796
00:29:25,940 --> 00:29:27,039
That's the idea.

797
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:29,069
"But that's very new."

798
00:29:29,070 --> 00:29:30,870
I wanted to make something like that.

799
00:29:30,940 --> 00:29:32,609
I invited a queen.

800
00:29:32,610 --> 00:29:33,779
(A special queen who'll join us for this performance)

801
00:29:33,780 --> 00:29:36,149
Funky Y, who'll be our secret weapon...

802
00:29:36,150 --> 00:29:38,110
and our Black Rose, will join us.

803
00:29:38,280 --> 00:29:42,389
(Funky Y, the leader of MANNEQUEEN, the queens of queens)

804
00:29:42,390 --> 00:29:45,589
I wanted to create this black rose, white rose theme.

805
00:29:45,590 --> 00:29:49,189
I've always collaborated a lot with Funky Y.

806
00:29:49,190 --> 00:29:51,859
During those collaborations, I felt we had chemistry.

807
00:29:51,860 --> 00:29:53,899
I wanted to show that on stage,

808
00:29:53,900 --> 00:29:55,929
so I cast Funky Y.

809
00:29:55,930 --> 00:29:57,600
We're going to do this sort of makeup.

810
00:29:58,270 --> 00:29:59,969
