00:42:26,080 --> 00:42:27,250
This is nice.

1078
00:42:30,950 --> 00:42:32,690
(Exclaiming)

1079
00:42:33,020 --> 00:42:34,319
(She's surprised.)

1080
00:42:34,320 --> 00:42:36,490
(Eyes on the stage)

1081
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:47,000
Nice!

1082
00:42:48,740 --> 00:42:51,170
She really used the projector well. She made them look like wings.

1083
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:56,650
There are wings.

1084
00:42:57,310 --> 00:42:58,910
Nice!

1085
00:43:02,950 --> 00:43:04,120
Nice!

1086
00:43:05,890 --> 00:43:07,390
The effects are amazing.

1087
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:10,589
- Nice.
- She wants to come out.

1088
00:43:10,590 --> 00:43:12,460
I think she's expressing something like oppression.

1089
00:43:26,640 --> 00:43:28,540
Her emotional progression is...

1090
00:43:46,060 --> 00:43:47,859
(Kim Hwan, Nemo, Jeong Bum, Na Hyun, Hwee Yul, Eun Seo, Ji Yul, Hui Rim)

1091
00:43:47,860 --> 00:43:48,899
(So Hyun, Yeon Woo, Kim Eun Jin)

1092
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:52,400
(Automatic applause)

1093
00:43:54,300 --> 00:43:55,739
It felt so refreshing.

1094
00:43:55,740 --> 00:43:57,340
I couldn't contain myself.

1095
00:43:57,410 --> 00:43:59,610
That feeling of being overwhelmed was different.

1096
00:44:00,610 --> 00:44:01,740
She did an amazing job.

1097
00:44:02,110 --> 00:44:03,949
- There were no mistakes.
- It was so cool.

1098
00:44:03,950 --> 00:44:05,550
Right. There were no mistakes.

1099
00:44:05,910 --> 00:44:08,149
Simeez did a great job.

1100
00:44:08,150 --> 00:44:10,350
It really messed with my head.

1101
00:44:10,450 --> 00:44:12,390
You have to get ready to get hyped.

1102
00:44:12,590 --> 00:44:14,389
We have to be sweating. I said we have to be sweating by 9:30pm.

1103
00:44:14,390 --> 00:44:15,659
Start sweating.

1104
00:44:15,660 --> 00:44:16,860
Work up a sweat.

1105
00:44:18,490 --> 00:44:21,129
What did the three Fight Judges...

1106
00:44:21,130 --> 00:44:22,870
think about the performance?

1107
00:44:23,030 --> 00:44:26,569
Let's hear their comments.

1108
00:44:26,570 --> 00:44:28,939
The projection mapping that created those massive wings...

1109
00:44:28,940 --> 00:44:32,240
was really impressive.

1110
00:44:32,310 --> 00:44:34,879
The way each person moved their umbrella...

1111
00:44:34,880 --> 00:44:37,749
felt almost like they were breathing.

1112
00:44:37,750 --> 00:44:42,120
It was so impressive how the umbrellas were delicately used.

1113
00:44:42,250 --> 00:44:44,219
I thought the use of the umbrellas...

1114
00:44:44,220 --> 00:44:46,559
really elevated the individual movements...

1115
00:44:46,560 --> 00:44:51,230
and brought a whole new level of detail to the music.

1116
00:44:51,330 --> 00:44:53,500
It was amazing.

1117
00:44:54,260 --> 00:44:56,369
The first thing I thought was that it felt refreshing.

1118
00:44:56,370 --> 00:44:58,799
I just did what I wanted to do.

1119
00:44:58,800 --> 00:45:00,599
I was satisfied...

1120
00:45:00,600 --> 00:45:02,169
because I showed them who I was.

1121
00:45:02,170 --> 00:45:05,039
As a director, I thought you did a great job...

1122
00:45:05,040 --> 00:45:08,579
conveying the different formations and concepts,

1123
00:45:08,580 --> 00:45:10,180
and I was completely immersed in the performance.

1124
00:45:10,710 --> 00:45:13,249
I thought there were a lot of clever choices...

1125
00:45:13,250 --> 00:45:15,449
that made the performance feel three-dimensional...

1126
00:45:15,450 --> 00:45:18,019
while also making the flat images stand out clearly.

1127
00:45:18,020 --> 00:45:20,819
You started with crossing the stage...

1128
00:45:20,820 --> 00:45:22,459
then coming into the center,

1129
00:45:22,460 --> 00:45:25,690
and I thought you used the projection element...

1130
00:45:25,790 --> 00:45:27,830
at a key moment.

1131
00:45:28,160 --> 00:45:30,869
I could really feel all the effort you put...

1132
00:45:30,870 --> 00:45:32,199
into making the performance as immersive as possible.

1133
00:45:32,200 --> 00:45:34,199
The dancers had such great chemistry,

1134
00:45:34,200 --> 00:45:36,609
and there were so many moments that felt like movie scenes,

1135
00:45:36,610 --> 00:45:37,910
which made the performance really dynamic.

1136
00:45:39,170 --> 00:45:40,640
Well done.

1137
00:45:42,410 --> 00:45:45,349
My elimination was at stake,

1138
00:45:45,350 --> 00:45:48,220
but when considering my performance, I thought I had a chance.

1139
00:45:48,720 --> 00:45:50,419
Personally, I think Simeez's performance...

1140
00:45:50,420 --> 00:45:52,920
stood out more than BADA's.

1141
00:45:53,120 --> 00:45:54,620
She used the props...

1142
00:45:54,720 --> 00:45:56,390
in a less conventional way.

1143
00:45:56,730 --> 00:45:58,859
It was nearly perfect.

1144
00:45:58,860 --> 00:46:01,160
I don't know. I think it's neck and neck.

1145
00:46:01,560 --> 00:46:04,399
(Simeez returns to the waiting room after the performance.)

1146
00:46:04,400 --> 00:46:05,930
Why is she crying so much?

1147
00:46:06,870 --> 00:46:07,939
What is it?

1148
00:46:07,940 --> 00:46:08,999
(Crying)

1149
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:10,409
What is it?

1150
00:46:10,410 --> 00:46:11,810
(Patting)

1151
00:46:12,070 --> 00:46:13,210
Why are you crying?

1152
00:46:13,880 --> 00:46:14,979
I think...

1153
00:46:14,980 --> 00:46:16,010
(I think I didn't do so well.)

1154
00:46:16,680 --> 00:46:17,949
I heard good comments.

1155
00:46:17,950 --> 00:46:19,679
- Shall we watch the next one?
- Okay.

1156
00:46:19,680 --> 00:46:21,350
- INGYOO's performance.
- We have to watch that one.

1157
00:46:21,580 --> 00:46:23,149
Well done, everyone!

1158
00:46:23,150 --> 00:46:25,050
(Well done!)

1159
00:46:25,890 --> 00:46:26,920
Let's watch it.

1160
00:46:27,420 --> 00:46:29,020
Let's watch INGYOO's performance!

1161
00:46:29,090 --> 00:46:31,430
Let's see how well he does.

1162
00:46:32,230 --> 00:46:35,660
The director to perform the last stage next...

1163
00:46:36,330 --> 00:46:37,570
is INGYOO.

1164
00:46:38,830 --> 00:46:40,499
Let's get it, Kim In Gyoo!

1165
00:46:40,500 --> 00:46:42,910
Let's go!

1166
00:46:43,410 --> 00:46:44,440
(Exclaiming)

1167
00:46:45,870 --> 00:46:47,340
He's covered in blood.

1168
00:46:47,940 --> 00:46:49,110
That's cool.

1169
00:46:49,210 --> 00:46:50,750
(They're looking forward to it.)

1170
00:46:50,850 --> 00:46:52,479
Let's go, INGYOO!

1171
00:46:52,480 --> 00:46:54,779
INGYOO's performances are always high quality,

1172
00:46:54,780 --> 00:46:55,879
so I was looking forward to it.

1173
00:46:55,880 --> 00:46:56,919
I have to win.

1174
00:46:56,920 --> 00:46:57,990
I will survive.

1175
00:46:58,090 --> 00:47:00,489
What did you want to show people...

1176
00:47:00,490 --> 00:47:02,659
as a director in the Last Stage?

1177
00:47:02,660 --> 00:47:03,889
Having fun?

1178
00:47:03,890 --> 00:47:05,259
In the end, this is a competition,

1179
00:47:05,260 --> 00:47:07,229
so we have to present performances to win.

1180
00:47:07,230 --> 00:47:08,999
But what I can do best...

1181
00:47:09,000 --> 00:47:10,199
is to enjoy it.

1182
00:47:10,200 --> 00:47:14,099
Through that, I want the judges and the audience...

1183
00:47:14,100 --> 00:47:15,670
to have fun as well.

1184
00:47:19,310 --> 00:47:20,580
Yes!

1185
00:47:20,640 --> 00:47:22,379
Something exciting and most fun.

1186
00:47:22,380 --> 00:47:24,550
Out of the four of us, I'm the best at having fun.

1187
00:47:24,680 --> 00:47:27,019
The overall concept is simple.

1188
00:47:27,020 --> 00:47:28,050
It's ninja.

1189
00:47:28,520 --> 00:47:30,950
But I didn't want to make it obvious.

1190
00:47:31,020 --> 00:47:32,089
Did you listen to the music?

1191
00:47:32,090 --> 00:47:33,159
I did.

1192
00:47:33,160 --> 00:47:34,790
- It's fine, isn't it?
- It was nice.

1193
00:47:34,890 --> 00:47:37,789
The song I'd like to request...

1194
00:47:37,790 --> 00:47:38,990
is an Amapiano track.

1195
00:47:39,390 --> 00:47:41,129
Amapiano...

1196
00:47:41,130 --> 00:47:44,999
is a style of music that's widely popular in South Africa.

1197
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:46,669
It's a genre I really like.

1198
00:47:46,670 --> 00:47:47,969
I thought it would be new to just have an umbrella...

1199
00:47:47,970 --> 00:47:50,170
with that music.

1200
00:47:50,370 --> 00:47:52,640
But I needed an interesting concept.

1201
00:47:52,840 --> 00:47:55,610
(INGYOO plays the track for the Last Stage.)

1202
00:47:56,850 --> 00:47:58,049
That's great.

1203
00:47:58,050 --> 00:47:59,150
The music is great.

1204
00:48:00,780 --> 00:48:02,950
(In a trance)

1205
00:48:03,750 --> 00:48:05,949
There was a point...

1206
00:48:05,950 --> 00:48:08,190
when the music started sounding Asian.

1207
00:48:08,990 --> 00:48:10,290
Shall we go with ninja?

1208
00:48:10,390 --> 00:48:12,130
- Ninja.
- Let's go!

1209
00:48:12,230 --> 00:48:13,329
Let's do it.

1210
00:48:13,330 --> 00:48:15,330
A ninja who uses spells.

1211
00:48:15,400 --> 00:48:17,669
It made me think of "Demon Slayer."

1212
00:48:17,670 --> 00:48:19,499
I really like Thunderclap and Flash.

1213
00:48:19,500 --> 00:48:20,839
Thunder Breathing is the best.

1214
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:23,569
I thought I could use that.

1215
00:48:23,570 --> 00:48:24,939
Try setting up the umbrellas unevenly.

1216
00:48:24,940 --> 00:48:26,410
Front and diagonal.

1217
00:48:26,510 --> 00:48:28,439
(Instant execution)

1218
00:48:28,440 --> 00:48:29,680
Try arranging them in a zigzag pattern.

1219
00:48:29,750 --> 00:48:32,650
(Using props to recreate ninja techniques from anime)

1220
00:48:33,580 --> 00:48:35,649
Show us that part.

1221
00:48:35,650 --> 00:48:36,919
Should I appear from there?

1222
00:48:36,920 --> 00:48:39,089
One, two, three, four.

1223
00:48:39,090 --> 00:48:40,160
Five.

1224
00:48:40,490 --> 00:48:43,090
No one can mix Amapiano with ninja.

1225
00:48:43,230 --> 00:48:46,059
Being able to blend these two...

1226
00:48:46,060 --> 00:48:47,599
is what what makes my directing strong.

1227
00:48:47,600 --> 00:48:50,029
Blending various things together...

1228
00:48:50,030 --> 00:48:51,729
and creating something new.

1229
00:48:51,730 --> 00:48:53,599
Also, I have fun...

1230
00:48:53,600 --> 00:48:54,740
when I make such new things.

1231
00:48:54,800 --> 00:48:58,169
I think INGYOO's concept really stands out too.

1232
00:48:58,170 --> 00:48:59,409
Right. Ninja.

1233
00:48:59,410 --> 00:49:00,940
It also goes well with WE DEM BOYZ.

1234
00:49:01,010 --> 00:49:02,510
That's something men like.

1235
00:49:02,740 --> 00:49:04,349
It gets our hearts racing.

1236
00:49:04,350 --> 00:49:05,550
How do you resist that?

1237
00:49:05,580 --> 00:49:06,779
INGYOO...

1238
00:49:06,780 --> 00:49:07,820
certainly is a genius.

1239
00:49:07,850 --> 00:49:09,520
I think INGYOO is the biggest threat to me.

1240
00:49:09,650 --> 00:49:11,889
Ninjas don't wear fancy clothes.

1241
00:49:11,890 --> 00:49:13,589
They have to stay hidden,

1242
00:49:13,590 --> 00:49:15,220
so they wear a head covering.

1243
00:49:15,360 --> 00:49:17,960
(Tearing and tearing)

1244
00:49:18,030 --> 00:49:19,360
(Tearing all the fabric)

1245
00:49:19,490 --> 00:49:21,560
We'll tie our sleeves and pant hems with strings.

1246
00:49:21,660 --> 00:49:24,129
This really shows our determination for the Last Stage.

1247
00:49:24,130 --> 00:49:25,570
It's so cool.

1248
00:49:25,830 --> 00:49:27,299
We look like ninjas.

1249
00:49:27,300 --> 00:49:28,870
- You look nice.
- Great.

1250
00:49:28,970 --> 00:49:30,710
How to be a ninja on a budget.

1251
00:49:30,810 --> 00:49:33,980
It'll be boring to wear just black for a performance.

1252
00:49:34,140 --> 00:49:35,609
So we put red body paint on...

1253
00:49:35,610 --> 00:49:37,310
to show that we're part of one big group.

1254
00:49:38,350 --> 00:49:40,350
(They put red contact lenses in too.)

1255
00:49:41,220 --> 00:49:43,250
(Transformation into ninjas complete)

1256
00:49:43,690 --> 00:49:46,419
Guys, let's sleep in once this is over.

1257
00:49:46,420 --> 00:49:47,989
You all did so well. We look awesome right now,

1258
00:49:47,990 --> 00:49:48,990
so let's have fun.

1259
00:49:48,991 --> 00:49:50,030
- Of course!
- Yes!

1260
00:49:50,090 --> 00:49:51,159
One, two, three!

1261
00:49:51,160 --> 00:49:52,890
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

1262
00:49:53,360 --> 00:49:55,230
- You got this.
- Break a leg.

1263
00:49:55,730 --> 00:49:57,699
INGYOO is really talented,

1264
00:49:57,700 --> 00:49:59,200
so I can't help but feel threatened.

1265
00:49:59,330 --> 00:50:00,440
Good luck!

1266
00:50:01,770 --> 00:50:03,040
Let's go and crush it out there.

1267
00:50:03,840 --> 00:50:05,139
I don't care about winning.

1268
00:50:05,140 --> 00:50:06,880
I just want us to look amazing out there.

1269
00:50:07,240 --> 00:50:08,540
I can't wait to dance.

1270
00:50:08,680 --> 00:50:10,410
I want everyone to see our performance.

1271
00:50:10,650 --> 00:50:12,249
- Let's go!
- Yes!

1272
00:50:12,250 --> 00:50:15,249
This is INGYOO's Last Stage that he prepared for 24 hours.

1273
00:50:15,250 --> 00:50:17,020
- You got this!
- Good luck!

1274
00:50:17,190 --> 00:50:18,789
Let's go!

1275
00:50:18,790 --> 00:50:20,590
Ready, fight!

1276
00:50:22,820 --> 00:50:24,329
(Amaninjas, Overall concept, Ninjas' victory dance)

1277
00:50:24,330 --> 00:50:25,690
(Objet strategy, using umbrellas as swords and weapons)

1278
00:50:25,930 --> 00:50:27,730
(Performance by Team Ninja)

1279
00:50:31,300 --> 00:50:32,330
Nice.

1280
00:50:35,500 --> 00:50:36,710
It's the canyon.

1281
00:50:40,040 --> 00:50:41,880
- It's a good setup.
- It's very exotic.

1282
00:50:42,040 --> 00:50:43,040
They put up bars.

1283
00:50:50,050 --> 00:50:51,050
Awesome.

1284
00:50:52,520 --> 00:50:53,960
This is already so fun.

1285
00:51:05,430 --> 00:51:06,570
That's so sexy!

1286
00:51:08,340 --> 00:51:10,510
Only WE DEM BOYZ can do this.

1287
00:51:14,880 --> 00:51:16,340
You're killing it!

1288
00:51:24,420 --> 00:51:25,490
Gosh!

1289
00:51:28,690 --> 00:51:30,090
They're so good.

1290
00:51:34,560 --> 00:51:35,700
They're incredible.

1291
00:51:46,980 --> 00:51:49,040
How he set up the running formation is just...

1292
00:51:52,080 --> 00:51:53,420
This is crazy.

1293
00:51:57,420 --> 00:51:59,190
- Amazing.
- The direction is so classy.

1294
00:52:00,120 --> 00:52:01,160
Goodness.

1295
00:52:01,860 --> 00:52:03,160
Thunderclap and Flash!

1296
00:52:03,290 --> 00:52:04,460
Isn't that from "Demon Slayer?"

1297
00:52:05,090 --> 00:52:06,600
(This is insane!)

1298
00:52:06,830 --> 00:52:09,100
(Electric)

1299
00:52:14,870 --> 00:52:16,240
This is astonishing.

1300
00:52:16,570 --> 00:52:17,670
They put away the umbrellas.

1301
00:52:19,340 --> 00:52:20,440
This is incredible.

1302
00:52:21,310 --> 00:52:22,480
INGYOO, you crushed it.

1303
00:52:25,910 --> 00:52:26,980
So fantastic!

1304
00:52:28,220 --> 00:52:29,950
This is very WE DEM BOYZ. It's so fun.

1305
00:52:40,300 --> 00:52:41,329
(Team INGYOO Dancers Kamel, AHOB, Youngbin, Dophan, NOAN)

1306
00:52:41,330 --> 00:52:42,359
(HOJUN, LIL LAW, Kwon Moo Joon, Park Ye Seong, Kim Woo Seok,)

1307
00:52:42,360 --> 00:52:43,429
(Lee Woo Jae, Kim Hyun Soo, Jung Tae Min)

1308
00:52:43,430 --> 00:52:45,069
This was so fun. We were the best.

1309
00:52:45,070 --> 00:52:46,570
It'll be hard to beat me.

1310
00:52:46,670 --> 00:52:49,040
(Loving it)

1311
00:52:49,340 --> 00:52:53,310
(Amazing)

1312
00:52:57,180 --> 00:52:59,080
- That was so cool.
- It was great!

1313
00:53:01,720 --> 00:53:02,720
So awesome.

1314
00:53:02,721 --> 00:53:05,190
How did he come up with this in 24 hours?

1315
00:53:05,220 --> 00:53:06,320
I was so in awe.

1316
00:53:07,060 --> 00:53:08,720
You look so handsome!

1317
00:53:09,160 --> 00:53:10,190
He crushed it.

1318
00:53:10,290 --> 00:53:12,989
There was a certain wit only INGYOO could pull off.

1319
00:53:12,990 --> 00:53:15,459
I'm curious what the three Fight Judges...

1320
00:53:15,460 --> 00:53:16,869
thought of this performance.

1321
00:53:16,870 --> 00:53:19,429
Let's hear what the Judges have to say.

1322
00:53:19,430 --> 00:53:22,470
First of all, INGYOO, that was amazing.

1323
00:53:24,970 --> 00:53:28,109
The key point was to utilize the umbrellas.

1324
00:53:28,110 --> 00:53:29,979
And how each directors used them...

1325
00:53:29,980 --> 00:53:33,979
would be the real attraction of the direction.

1326
00:53:33,980 --> 00:53:37,790
But I thought you wouldn't need them at all.

1327
00:53:38,790 --> 00:53:40,120
It worked.

1328
00:53:40,260 --> 00:53:43,430
And you threw away the umbrellas, like you were proving my point.

1329
00:53:48,800 --> 00:53:50,070
That was just amazing.

1330
00:53:50,130 --> 00:53:52,499
Throwing them away was Akane's type.

1331
00:53:52,500 --> 00:53:54,470
They all got so much better after tossing the umbrellas.

1332
00:53:56,300 --> 00:53:59,539
And as for the choreography,

1333
00:53:59,540 --> 00:54:02,339
I was surprised to see how you used different dance techniques...

1334
00:54:02,340 --> 00:54:04,849
throughout the performance in a unique way.

1335
00:54:04,850 --> 00:54:06,780
Overall, it was amazing.

1336
00:54:09,850 --> 00:54:12,649
I really liked the lighting at the beginning.

1337
00:54:12,650 --> 00:54:13,859
The moment it began,

1338
00:54:13,860 --> 00:54:17,389
I got the sense that I was entering another world.

1339
00:54:17,390 --> 00:54:19,130
I was visiting a ninja castle.

1340
00:54:19,190 --> 00:54:22,360
And your use of projections was impressive.

1341
00:54:25,430 --> 00:54:26,899
I got the sense that...

1342
00:54:26,900 --> 00:54:29,339
you were trying to leave a big impact by using them once.

1343
00:54:29,340 --> 00:54:33,040
That alone was very impactful for me.

1344
00:54:33,140 --> 00:54:35,779
What was interesting was that your concept...

1345
00:54:35,780 --> 00:54:38,449
is ninjas, which are East Asian and can be somewhat oriental.

1346
00:54:38,450 --> 00:54:40,849
But you used African beats with Amapiano style.

1347
00:54:40,850 --> 00:54:43,319
It could've been a strange match,

1348
00:54:43,320 --> 00:54:47,019
but it made me wonder if I could've thought of this as well.

1349
00:54:47,020 --> 00:54:48,219
You put it together beautifully.

1350
00:54:48,220 --> 00:54:51,159
And some of your dancers on stage...

1351
00:54:51,160 --> 00:54:52,860
made the mistake of...

1352
00:54:53,030 --> 00:54:55,700
dropping their umbrellas from the start.

1353
00:54:55,960 --> 00:54:58,870
For me, mistakes don't really matter too much.

1354
00:54:59,030 --> 00:55:00,700
That's because I was still immersed.

1355
00:55:00,870 --> 00:55:04,570
That alone was meaningful for me.

1356
00:55:05,070 --> 00:55:08,109
INGYOO pulled an INGYOO.

1357
00:55:08,110 --> 00:55:09,240
Thank you for the performance.

1358
00:55:11,650 --> 00:55:13,379
I don't care much about mistakes either.

1359
00:55:13,380 --> 00:55:15,179
I care what happens after the mistake.

1360
00:55:15,180 --> 00:55:17,489
But after the mistake, the dancer...

1361
00:55:17,490 --> 00:55:20,119
kept on dancing like he was really holding a sword.

1362
00:55:20,120 --> 00:55:21,690
That pulled me back in.

1363
00:55:21,790 --> 00:55:24,859
The fact that you brought in a dancer with such skills...

1364
00:55:24,860 --> 00:55:27,699
shows how much talent you have, INGYOO.

1365
00:55:27,700 --> 00:55:30,069
I know you're much smarter...

1366
00:55:30,070 --> 00:55:32,430
than you let on, INGYOO.

1367
00:55:33,100 --> 00:55:36,100
And I think you showed another side of your genius today.

1368
00:55:36,200 --> 00:55:38,269
The entrances were very three-dimensional,

1369
00:55:38,270 --> 00:55:39,609
using follow spotlight.

1370
00:55:39,610 --> 00:55:41,979
It felt like I was in an animation,

1371
00:55:41,980 --> 00:55:43,780
and I couldn't look away.

1372
00:55:43,950 --> 00:55:45,950
I really appreciate how you put this together.

1373
00:55:46,780 --> 00:55:48,880
And you're very stylish, INGYOO.

1374
00:55:50,350 --> 00:55:52,819
I loved that she said I was stylish.

1375
00:55:52,820 --> 00:55:54,060
It was such an honor.

1376
00:55:57,890 --> 00:55:58,890
You did well.

1377
00:55:59,260 --> 00:56:00,460
Good job, INGYOO.

1378
00:56:01,060 --> 00:56:02,260
Way to go.

1379
00:56:03,500 --> 00:56:04,500
It's over.

1380
00:56:06,270 --> 00:56:08,269
- You did amazing!
- It's INGYOO!

1381
00:56:08,270 --> 00:56:09,270
(Shouting)

1382
00:56:11,270 --> 00:56:13,109
- Guys, great job. Bring it in.
- INGYOO!

1383
00:56:13,110 --> 00:56:15,510
We tied up the loose ends in there.

1384
00:56:15,610 --> 00:56:19,010
We put all that work into a minute and 30 seconds...

1385
00:56:19,150 --> 00:56:21,379
and blew people's minds in there!

1386
00:56:21,380 --> 00:56:22,380
That's all there is to it.

1387
00:56:22,381 --> 00:56:23,820
Great work, guys. I had so much fun.

1388
00:56:24,220 --> 00:56:25,320
Great work!

1389
00:56:25,920 --> 00:56:27,160
INGYOO pulled an INGYOO.

1390
00:56:27,860 --> 00:56:29,220
I still got it.

1391
00:56:29,760 --> 00:56:31,730
"Street World Fighter: Directors' War".

1392
00:56:31,890 --> 00:56:34,900
The last director to present their Last Stage...

1393
00:56:35,260 --> 00:56:36,770
is JEONG MIN JUN.

1394
00:56:36,800 --> 00:56:38,730
(Finally)

1395
00:56:40,070 --> 00:56:41,370
(He's here!)

1396
00:56:41,440 --> 00:56:42,739
At last.

1397
00:56:42,740 --> 00:56:43,840
Gosh.

1398
00:56:44,170 --> 00:56:46,009
I'm most worried about MIN JUN.

1399
00:56:46,010 --> 00:56:48,239
He became the master of the Last Stage.

1400
00:56:48,240 --> 00:56:49,639
(JEONG MIN JUN steps onto the stage.)

1401
00:56:49,640 --> 00:56:52,080
(He's wearing something peculiar today as usual.)

1402
00:56:52,150 --> 00:56:53,350
I wonder what his concept is.

1403
00:56:53,920 --> 00:56:56,650
(The crowd is shocked by his strange attire.)

1404
00:56:57,850 --> 00:56:59,890
He cut up his clothes too much.

1405
00:57:00,320 --> 00:57:01,490
But it suits him somehow.

1406
00:57:01,920 --> 00:57:03,629
Once this performance is over,

1407
00:57:03,630 --> 00:57:05,789
the winner and loser will be determined.

1408
00:57:05,790 --> 00:57:08,460
As a director, what's the one thing you want to show...

1409
00:57:08,630 --> 00:57:10,870
in this Last Stage?

1410
00:57:11,030 --> 00:57:13,970
There are so many stories I love.

1411
00:57:14,140 --> 00:57:16,399
And I want to be a director...

1412
00:57:16,400 --> 00:57:18,170
that conveys those stories...

1413
00:57:18,340 --> 00:57:20,440
to the people watching.

1414
00:57:20,910 --> 00:57:23,479
If you watch all the performances I've made so far,

1415
00:57:23,480 --> 00:57:25,450
there's always drama it.

1416
00:57:26,050 --> 00:57:27,050
There's a plot.

1417
00:57:27,051 --> 00:57:28,980
For the first Last Stage,

1418
00:57:29,020 --> 00:57:31,290
I used a historic battle as motivation.

1419
00:57:31,350 --> 00:57:32,789
For the second one,

1420
00:57:32,790 --> 00:57:34,319
there was a bit of desperation.

1421
00:57:34,320 --> 00:57:36,990
And I tried to use that in the performance.

1422
00:57:37,130 --> 00:57:40,090
I think the director's job is to...

1423
00:57:40,260 --> 00:57:43,299
convey the narrative to the viewers...

1424
00:57:43,300 --> 00:57:44,769
and make them understand.

1425
00:57:44,770 --> 00:57:47,370
In that sense, I really put in a lot of work.

1426
00:57:47,500 --> 00:57:48,939
I'm sure MIN JUN has a plan.

1427
00:57:48,940 --> 00:57:50,910
Yes, I thought it through this time.

1428
00:57:51,240 --> 00:57:53,340
I knew I'd be on the Last Stage.

1429
00:57:53,510 --> 00:57:54,680
What's the concept this time?

1430
00:57:54,880 --> 00:57:55,880
"The Odyssey".

1431
00:57:56,110 --> 00:57:57,609
(That's MIN JUN.)

1432
00:57:57,610 --> 00:57:59,010
- Gosh.
- You're so trendy.

1433
00:57:59,750 --> 00:58:01,579
I recently watched the film, "The Odyssey,"

1434
00:58:01,580 --> 00:58:03,520
and I was really inspired by it.

1435
00:58:03,850 --> 00:58:06,449
I just knew I had to make it the concept...

1436
00:58:06,450 --> 00:58:08,220
for the Last Stage.

1437
00:58:08,590 --> 00:58:10,459
Who wants to try this?

1438
00:58:10,460 --> 00:58:12,560
Hold the umbrella and do a sword fight.

1439
00:58:12,890 --> 00:58:14,429
The first image I had...

1440
00:58:14,430 --> 00:58:16,499
with an umbrella was weapons.

1441
00:58:16,500 --> 00:58:19,269
And since I had to use many umbrellas,

1442
00:58:19,270 --> 00:58:21,040
it made me think of an army.

1443
00:58:21,100 --> 00:58:23,470
That led me to the concept of war.

1444
00:58:23,640 --> 00:58:25,370
First, you open the umbrella...

1445
00:58:26,070 --> 00:58:27,139
and huddle.

1446
00:58:27,140 --> 00:58:29,839
We're going to make a shape like the Trojan horse.

1447
00:58:29,840 --> 00:58:31,709
Since we're going with "The Odyssey,"

1448
00:58:31,710 --> 00:58:34,280
I thought we'd have to use the Trojan horse at some point.

1449
00:58:34,350 --> 00:58:37,219
And if we positioned the umbrellas to look like the horse...

1450
00:58:37,220 --> 00:58:39,489
and used a projector...

1451
00:58:39,490 --> 00:58:42,819
to shoot wooden textures onto the umbrellas,

1452
00:58:42,820 --> 00:58:45,489
with tree rings and whatnot...

1453
00:58:45,490 --> 00:58:48,159
And if we had human silhouettes showing...

1454
00:58:48,160 --> 00:58:49,900
in between the shape,

1455
00:58:50,400 --> 00:58:51,669
I'm sure the people would think...

1456
00:58:51,670 --> 00:58:53,900
that it's the Trojan horse.

1457
00:58:54,140 --> 00:58:57,039
I've been talking with the musical director as well.

1458
00:58:57,040 --> 00:58:59,170
I want drums to go wild...

1459
00:58:59,270 --> 00:59:00,679
at some point.

1460
00:59:00,680 --> 00:59:03,039
I think at first, we could take it steady...

1461
00:59:03,040 --> 00:59:04,410
until the middle.

1462
00:59:04,580 --> 00:59:06,920
And we could make it blow up in the end.

1463
00:59:07,520 --> 00:59:10,119
I wanted to utilize military-type beats...

1464
00:59:10,120 --> 00:59:12,650
like in "The Odyssey" into the song.

1465
00:59:13,090 --> 00:59:14,859
- Let's see.
- It's much nicer, right?

1466
00:59:14,860 --> 00:59:16,319
- It really is.
- Good.

1467
00:59:16,320 --> 00:59:20,060
I wanted ancient Northern European styles for hair and makeup as well.

1468
00:59:20,130 --> 00:59:22,399
"The Odyssey" is set in ancient times.

1469
00:59:22,400 --> 00:59:24,230
I wanted to portray that in the costume.

1470
00:59:24,270 --> 00:59:26,030
(He changes into the costume.)

1471
00:59:27,000 --> 00:59:28,000
(Exclaiming)

1472
00:59:28,001 --> 00:59:29,499
You look like a rich beggar.

1473
00:59:29,500 --> 00:59:31,010
What is this concept?

1474
00:59:31,340 --> 00:59:32,639
It's "The Odyssey".

1475
00:59:32,640 --> 00:59:36,080
So I kept the hair and makeup to a minimum.

1476
00:59:36,210 --> 00:59:38,410
- I want to look like a wanderer.
- Wanderer, got it.

1477
00:59:39,250 --> 00:59:41,919
You'll look cool once you get into your performance.

1478
00:59:41,920 --> 00:59:43,690
I just want to put on a great performance,

1479
00:59:43,850 --> 00:59:46,619
and connect with the audience with my performance.

1480
00:59:46,620 --> 00:59:48,190
I'm sure I can make it happen.

1481
00:59:49,990 --> 00:59:52,690
JEONG MIN JUN prepared this Last Stage...

1482
00:59:52,760 --> 00:59:56,099
for 24 hours to survive this competition.

1483
00:59:56,100 --> 00:59:57,130
Ready?

1484
00:59:57,500 --> 00:59:58,570
Fight!

1485
01:00:02,000 --> 01:00:04,139
- Let's go!
- We love you!

1486
01:00:04,140 --> 01:00:05,670
(Let's go, JEONG MIN JUN!)

1487
01:00:06,010 --> 01:00:07,680
(Flipping)

1488
01:00:07,910 --> 01:00:09,580
(Startled)

1489
01:00:10,180 --> 01:00:12,150
(They're turning the umbrellas inside out.)

1490
01:00:14,120 --> 01:00:16,020
- They're holding it differently.
- I like that they turned it over.

1491
01:00:16,120 --> 01:00:17,120
I know, right?

1492
01:00:17,121 --> 01:00:18,420
(What performance will they show us with the upturned umbrellas?)

1493
01:00:18,850 --> 01:00:20,689
This is my third Last Stage.

1494
01:00:20,690 --> 01:00:22,160
I think I mastered it at this point.

1495
01:00:22,220 --> 01:00:24,690
I'll have an edge.

1496
01:00:27,200 --> 01:00:28,559
(Odyssey, Overall concept, The story of Odysseus' war)

1497
01:00:28,560 --> 01:00:29,900
(Objet stragegy, reflecting light and forming a Trojan horse)

1498
01:00:30,200 --> 01:00:32,000
(Performance by Team JEONG MIN JUN)

1499
01:00:35,100 --> 01:00:36,500
(Surprised)

1500
01:01:00,400 --> 01:01:02,760
- This is legendary.
- It looks so cool.

1501
01:01:32,590 --> 01:01:34,230
MIN JUN is killing it.

1502
01:01:48,840 --> 01:01:50,310
That's his trademark move!

1503
01:01:58,650 --> 01:02:00,020
That's incredible.

1504
01:02:00,520 --> 01:02:03,390
(Engrossed)

1505
01:02:03,960 --> 01:02:05,090
It's like a film.

1506
01:02:05,660 --> 01:02:06,690
This is amazing.

1507
01:02:19,970 --> 01:02:21,040
He's being taken.

1508
01:02:27,850 --> 01:02:28,949
(Team JEONG MIN JUN Dancers)

1509
01:02:28,950 --> 01:02:30,079
(JYOS, Noah Im, Heejae, Jaeyoon, Jungmin, HAN, Harang, KUNA,)

1510
01:02:30,080 --> 01:02:31,150
(GUMA, Kwon Ian, Hasom, EVE, murphy, Go Ara)

1511
01:02:31,350 --> 01:02:34,520
(Cheering fills the entire set.)

1512
01:02:35,660 --> 01:02:36,660
(Exclaiming)

1513
01:02:36,661 --> 01:02:37,689
That was amazing.

1514
01:02:37,690 --> 01:02:38,690
Respect!

1515
01:02:39,190 --> 01:02:40,230
Gosh.

1516
01:02:42,130 --> 01:02:44,800
I did it. I'm so glad it went just the way I imagined.

1517
01:02:48,000 --> 01:02:49,940
MIN JUN was too good. I'm really worried.

1518
01:02:50,240 --> 01:02:52,040
MIN JUN is definitely going to survive again.

1519
01:02:52,540 --> 01:02:53,839
What did...

1520
01:02:53,840 --> 01:02:57,079
the three Fight Judges think of this performance?

1521
01:02:57,080 --> 01:03:00,280
Let's hear their comments right now.

1522
01:03:00,410 --> 01:03:03,849
First of all, I think your direction capability is amazing.

1523
01:03:03,850 --> 01:03:06,149
You can't get people to cheer this loudly otherwise.

1524
01:03:06,150 --> 01:03:10,260
And I have a nickname for you, MIN JUN.

1525
01:03:10,930 --> 01:03:13,760
Intro Genius.

1526
01:03:14,400 --> 01:03:16,200
You're an Intro Genius.

1527
01:03:16,960 --> 01:03:19,270
(A unique intro like no other)

1528
01:03:21,600 --> 01:03:23,740
You're truly an artist.

1529
01:03:23,940 --> 01:03:25,969
It was such an amazing performance.

1530
01:03:25,970 --> 01:03:27,339
Picturing it in your head...

1531
01:03:27,340 --> 01:03:29,039
and succeeding in bringing it to life are two different things.

1532
01:03:29,040 --> 01:03:30,780
Amazing work.

1533
01:03:33,250 --> 01:03:34,780
I was so glad she noticed my hard work.

1534
01:03:34,920 --> 01:03:36,080
I was elated.

1535
01:03:36,250 --> 01:03:39,890
What I first noticed...

1536
01:03:39,950 --> 01:03:43,959
while watching your performance was...

1537
01:03:43,960 --> 01:03:46,629
your desire to move the audience's feelings.

1538
01:03:46,630 --> 01:03:48,559
That's what made this more impressive.

1539
01:03:48,560 --> 01:03:49,660
Thank you.

1540
01:03:54,240 --> 01:03:58,009
The most creative use of the objets...

1541
01:03:58,010 --> 01:03:59,639
was the Trojan horse,

1542
01:03:59,640 --> 01:04:03,309
and the human silhouette after that.

1543
01:04:03,310 --> 01:04:04,809
I was really impressed with that.

1544
01:04:04,810 --> 01:04:07,749
But I did have some disappointments.

1545
01:04:07,750 --> 01:04:09,649
The way you expressed your ideas was creative,

1546
01:04:09,650 --> 01:04:11,989
but because you had such a firm idea for it,

1547
01:04:11,990 --> 01:04:15,290
I kept watching while wondering what it meant.

1548
01:04:15,390 --> 01:04:16,919
I thought it was a little superficial...

1549
01:04:16,920 --> 01:04:19,989
to portray the concept of the Odyssey.

1550
01:04:19,990 --> 01:04:21,030
Thank you.

1551
01:04:25,130 --> 01:04:27,440
- You did well.
- Well done.

1552
01:04:27,570 --> 01:04:30,670
MIN JUN finished his third Last Stage.

1553
01:04:30,840 --> 01:04:32,369
Please give it up for MIN JUN...

1554
01:04:32,370 --> 01:04:34,280
for this incredible performance.

1555
01:04:35,480 --> 01:04:36,480
(You did...)

1556
01:04:36,481 --> 01:04:37,510
(so well!)

1557
01:04:37,710 --> 01:04:39,350
- Good job!
- Well done!

1558
01:04:43,850 --> 01:04:44,890
BADA!

1559
01:04:46,290 --> 01:04:47,520
Good work.

1560
01:04:49,490 --> 01:04:50,759
Whatever the outcome,

1561
01:04:50,760 --> 01:04:53,629
I did my very best, so I have no regrets.

1562
01:04:53,630 --> 01:04:56,130
I felt liberated.

1563
01:04:57,330 --> 01:05:00,599
The competition of "Street World Fighter: Directors' War"...

1564
01:05:00,600 --> 01:05:02,840
is coming to an end.

1565
01:05:04,110 --> 01:05:05,339
It's terrifying, really.

1566
01:05:05,340 --> 01:05:06,840
My hands get all sweaty.

1567
01:05:07,410 --> 01:05:08,780
I can't lose anyone.

1568
01:05:09,180 --> 01:05:10,880
No one deserves to go home.

1569
01:05:13,150 --> 01:05:14,419
(The 4 directors come on stage after their performance.)

1570
01:05:14,420 --> 01:05:15,720
Good job!

1571
01:05:16,450 --> 01:05:17,550
- Great work!
- Yes!

1572
01:05:18,050 --> 01:05:20,790
These directors have gone through many missions...

1573
01:05:20,960 --> 01:05:22,089
and two Last Stages...

1574
01:05:22,090 --> 01:05:24,930
for the position of the best director.

1575
01:05:25,090 --> 01:05:26,730
After their fierce competition,

1576
01:05:26,860 --> 01:05:30,500
these four directors stand at a crossroads of survival again.

1577
01:05:31,230 --> 01:05:32,700
Only two directors...

1578
01:05:32,830 --> 01:05:36,500
will survive today to make it to the semi-finals.

1579
01:05:36,940 --> 01:05:38,270
You're crying!

1580
01:05:39,510 --> 01:05:41,680
Why am I crying? I was overwhelmed.

1581
01:05:42,910 --> 01:05:45,150
Could I have a tissue? I didn't feel very confident.

1582
01:05:45,280 --> 01:05:47,109
My competitors were too great,

1583
01:05:47,110 --> 01:05:48,520
and I wasn't sure if I could beat them.

1584
01:05:48,750 --> 01:05:51,150
The anxiety is always there.

1585
01:05:51,750 --> 01:05:52,750
(Sighing)

1586
01:05:53,250 --> 01:05:54,520
My heart keeps pounding.

1587
01:05:54,660 --> 01:05:56,120
If you had fun, it's all good.

1588
01:05:56,790 --> 01:05:58,589
I want to go with INGYOO or Hee Jung.

1589
01:05:58,590 --> 01:05:59,929
I thought differently.

1590
01:05:59,930 --> 01:06:01,299
One of them used such an unexpected layout...

1591
01:06:01,300 --> 01:06:03,800
and really impressed me.

1592
01:06:04,070 --> 01:06:06,000
BADA's performance was the most polished.

1593
01:06:06,570 --> 01:06:08,839
I don't want to say it was ordinary,

1594
01:06:08,840 --> 01:06:13,869
but I have seen that direction somewhere before.

1595
01:06:13,870 --> 01:06:16,739
Wait a second. Let me ask you a question.

1596
01:06:16,740 --> 01:06:18,709
BADA had better quality,

1597
01:06:18,710 --> 01:06:20,349
but Hee Jung was the one who challenged herself.

1598
01:06:20,350 --> 01:06:24,189
I think Akane is looking at this in a different way than Monika,

1599
01:06:24,190 --> 01:06:26,549
and I admit I'm looking at this in another way too.

1600
01:06:26,550 --> 01:06:27,660
(The judges needed a lot of time.)

1601
01:06:27,790 --> 01:06:30,560
The last stage before the finals, the semi-finals.

1602
01:06:31,390 --> 01:06:34,659
Who will be the two directors...

1603
01:06:34,660 --> 01:06:36,730
to put their names on that stage?

1604
01:06:37,060 --> 01:06:40,000
I really want to win for the sake of my team.

1605
01:06:40,430 --> 01:06:42,500
I felt really free at first.

1606
01:06:42,670 --> 01:06:45,540
And I was taking it easy.

1607
01:06:45,940 --> 01:06:48,040
I had fun, so it's all good. I was satisfied.

1608
01:06:49,080 --> 01:06:51,850
The third Last Stage: 24H.

1609
01:06:52,680 --> 01:06:54,520
The first survivor is...

1610
01:06:56,480 --> 01:06:57,520
This is terrifying.

1611
01:06:57,750 --> 01:06:59,250
I really have no idea.

1612
01:07:00,390 --> 01:07:02,020
(Tension fills the studio.)

1613
01:07:03,360 --> 01:07:04,389
Director...

1614
01:07:04,390 --> 01:07:06,690
(Director...)

1615
01:07:06,890 --> 01:07:10,229
(Who is the first survivor to make it to the semi-finals?)

1616
01:07:10,230 --> 01:07:11,370
BADA.

1617
01:07:13,570 --> 01:07:15,970
(It's Director BADA.)

1618
01:07:20,980 --> 01:07:22,909
(The first survivor is BADA.)

1619
01:07:22,910 --> 01:07:27,309
I knew at first sight that it was a flower bud,

1620
01:07:27,310 --> 01:07:29,879
and I liked how she used each umbrella...

1621
01:07:29,880 --> 01:07:31,750
as a flower petal.

1622
01:07:31,890 --> 01:07:34,220
It was a very high-quality performance.

1623
01:07:34,690 --> 01:07:37,729
BADA's the one who used the objets...

1624
01:07:37,730 --> 01:07:38,830
- to the fullest.
- That's right.

1625
01:07:39,830 --> 01:07:41,329
The BADA we knew used to do...

1626
01:07:41,330 --> 01:07:44,030
androgynous performances.

1627
01:07:44,170 --> 01:07:46,400
Putting on a feminine performance must've been...

1628
01:07:46,500 --> 01:07:48,640
a huge challenge for her.

1629
01:07:48,740 --> 01:07:50,399
And she even managed to make it perfect.

1630
01:07:50,400 --> 01:07:51,410
You're right.

1631
01:07:53,510 --> 01:07:57,580
First, I want to thank the amazing three directors...

1632
01:07:57,750 --> 01:07:59,980
who put on the Last Stage with me.

1633
01:08:00,210 --> 01:08:02,620
Thank you for your hard work.

1634
01:08:02,780 --> 01:08:04,019
I'll show you more amazing...

1635
01:08:04,020 --> 01:08:07,459
and more BADA-like performances in the future.

1636
01:08:07,460 --> 01:08:08,490
Thank you!

1637
01:08:12,560 --> 01:08:14,400
Congratulations, BADA.

1638
01:08:14,830 --> 01:08:15,860
Well done.

1639
01:08:16,430 --> 01:08:18,130
You did so well.

1640
01:08:18,770 --> 01:08:22,070
I felt so sorry for the others that I made it...

1641
01:08:22,500 --> 01:08:25,039
to the next round safely on my own first.

1642
01:08:25,040 --> 01:08:27,170
We all put in so much work together.

1643
01:08:27,840 --> 01:08:30,980
I felt guilty, since we all did our best.

1644
01:08:32,350 --> 01:08:36,380
There is only one spot left in the semi-finals.

1645
01:08:37,080 --> 01:08:40,590
What will happen to the remaining three?

1646
01:08:41,160 --> 01:08:44,990
I will announce the first director to be eliminated...

1647
01:08:45,730 --> 01:08:48,430
in the third Last Stage: 24H.

1648
01:08:48,700 --> 01:08:50,870
Now it's a 33 percent chance.

1649
01:08:51,970 --> 01:08:53,930
I did what I wanted to do,

1650
01:08:54,130 --> 01:08:55,900
and I showed them who I am.

1651
01:08:56,000 --> 01:08:58,640
I was willing to accept my fate.

1652
01:08:59,410 --> 01:09:01,980
MIN JUN's direction was off the charts,

1653
01:09:02,480 --> 01:09:05,250
but if you look at the overall structure, mine was grander.

1654
01:09:05,580 --> 01:09:06,849
I was feeling good.

1655
01:09:06,850 --> 01:09:09,020
I was sure I'd pass this round.

1656
01:09:09,850 --> 01:09:11,620
"Street World Fighter: Directors' War".

1657
01:09:12,020 --> 01:09:16,090
The first director to be eliminated from the third Last Stage is...

1658
01:09:24,300 --> 01:09:25,769
It is JEONG MIN JUN.

1659
01:09:25,770 --> 01:09:27,469
(First eliminated choreographer, JEONG MIN JUN)

1660
01:09:27,470 --> 01:09:28,769
(Eliminated choreographer, JEONG MIN JUN)

1661
01:09:28,770 --> 01:09:32,810
(Shocking)

1662
01:09:36,240 --> 01:09:38,009
The expressive quality is really good,

1663
01:09:38,010 --> 01:09:40,919
but unless you look at the synopsis, it's hard to follow along...

1664
01:09:40,920 --> 01:09:43,879
It falls a bit short when it comes to expressing that aspect itself.

1665
01:09:43,880 --> 01:09:46,219
Since he has such a strong worldview,

1666
01:09:46,220 --> 01:09:49,090
I feel like he didn't choose more intuitive ways to express it.

1667
01:09:49,160 --> 01:09:51,429
However, though,

1668
01:09:51,430 --> 01:09:57,029
the fact that MIN JUN kept doing the same sort of thing every time,

1669
01:09:57,030 --> 01:09:58,329
bothered me a little.

1670
01:09:58,330 --> 01:10:00,329
Being a director isn't just about excelling in one area.

1671
01:10:00,330 --> 01:10:02,139
It requires proficiency across multiple aspects.

1672
01:10:02,140 --> 01:10:04,199
So, when the concepts remain consistently similar,

1673
01:10:04,200 --> 01:10:06,609
- the director's capabilities...
- You lack competence.

1674
01:10:06,610 --> 01:10:08,780
tends to come across as a shortcoming.

1675
01:10:09,540 --> 01:10:11,849
Please share a few final words.

1676
01:10:11,850 --> 01:10:13,379
(Third Last Stage: 24H Final elimination, MIN JUN)

1677
01:10:13,380 --> 01:10:15,819
(Well...)

1678
01:10:15,820 --> 01:10:16,980
For me...

1679
01:10:17,520 --> 01:10:21,520
this Last Stage was especially meaningful...

1680
01:10:21,860 --> 01:10:25,129
because the movie I watched...

1681
01:10:25,130 --> 01:10:27,330
with others was "Odyssey." But...

1682
01:10:27,860 --> 01:10:30,329
I personally cherished the conversations...

1683
01:10:30,330 --> 01:10:33,369
we shared after that,

1684
01:10:33,370 --> 01:10:37,840
and I really want to say that it was such a happy experience for me.

1685
01:10:38,410 --> 01:10:42,410
To be honest, when I first appeared on this program, I really hoped...

1686
01:10:42,640 --> 01:10:46,509
given that I work as a co-director for the team "The Stories,"

1687
01:10:46,510 --> 01:10:50,349
was that the competition scene I love so much...

1688
01:10:50,350 --> 01:10:54,419
would become known to a wider audience was my expectation.

1689
01:10:54,420 --> 01:10:57,359
I wondered if appearing on the show would really help get the word out.

1690
01:10:57,360 --> 01:11:01,129
I was quite worried about it,

1691
01:11:01,130 --> 01:11:03,329
but looking back, I feel I was able to show so much...

1692
01:11:03,330 --> 01:11:05,599
by participating in this program.

1693
01:11:05,600 --> 01:11:07,699
And ultimately, I feel I've shown...

1694
01:11:07,700 --> 01:11:11,369
the kind of director I am...

1695
01:11:11,370 --> 01:11:12,840
and the type of work I create,

1696
01:11:13,070 --> 01:11:16,340
so I think I've achieved everything I set out to do on this program.

1697
01:11:16,810 --> 01:11:20,109
The stories I'll be writing from here on out are...

1698
01:11:20,110 --> 01:11:22,020
just beginning,

1699
01:11:22,550 --> 01:11:24,049
so I hope you'll stay tuned.

1700
01:11:24,050 --> 01:11:25,050
(Please stay tuned for MIN JUN's new stories.)

1701
01:11:26,720 --> 01:11:27,920
Well done.

1702
01:11:28,160 --> 01:11:29,619
You did well. Really.

1703
01:11:29,620 --> 01:11:31,130
You know you did great, right?

1704
01:11:32,460 --> 01:11:35,500
(Well done, youngest one.)

1705
01:11:36,730 --> 01:11:38,369
(Eliminated choreographer, JEONG MIN JUN)

1706
01:11:38,370 --> 01:11:40,070
This is too hard, seriously.

1707
01:11:41,300 --> 01:11:44,670
Now, only the results for the last two people remain.

1708
01:11:44,970 --> 01:11:47,109
The final director to survive from...

1709
01:11:47,110 --> 01:11:50,180
"Street World Fighter: Directors' War Last Stage: 24H"...

1710
01:11:50,680 --> 01:11:53,480
and to advance to the semi-finals is...

1711
01:11:59,190 --> 01:12:00,250
(Last Stage: 24H, Simeez vs. INGYOO)

1712
01:12:00,490 --> 01:12:01,960
I think it's Simeez.

1713
01:12:02,190 --> 01:12:03,890
I think it was fantastic.

1714
01:12:04,430 --> 01:12:07,560
If they don't mind making mistakes, I think they'd choose INGYOO.

1715
01:12:07,730 --> 01:12:10,760
The introduction at the beginning was very good.

1716
01:12:11,300 --> 01:12:13,670
And I think he used the objet with more sensitivity.

1717
01:12:13,970 --> 01:12:16,040
I thought, "I'd win."

1718
01:12:17,300 --> 01:12:19,110
Whatever. Come what may.

1719
01:12:19,810 --> 01:12:21,109
(Which director will advance to the semi-finals...)

1720
01:12:21,110 --> 01:12:22,879
(after conquering the last stage?)

1721
01:12:22,880 --> 01:12:24,180
It is INGYOO.

1722
01:12:24,510 --> 01:12:28,149
(The second survivor, INGYOO)

1723
01:12:28,150 --> 01:12:31,350
(The second survivor, INGYOO)

1724
01:12:32,420 --> 01:12:33,649
Congratulations, INGYOO.

1725
01:12:33,650 --> 01:12:37,160
(Third Last Stage: 24H Final elimination, Simeez)

1726
01:12:38,990 --> 01:12:40,929
It struck the perfect balance...

1727
01:12:40,930 --> 01:12:44,599
between an oriental aesthetic and a trendy vibe.

1728
01:12:44,600 --> 01:12:47,770
Plus, you couldn't tell at all that he made a mistake with the umbrella.

1729
01:12:48,570 --> 01:12:50,899
When it comes to making the most of the stage and the lighting,

1730
01:12:50,900 --> 01:12:52,570
he was the first, to be honest.

1731
01:12:52,940 --> 01:12:56,179
If you ask whose work I'd like to see more of in the future,

1732
01:12:56,180 --> 01:12:57,540
I think it would be INGYOO's.

1733
01:12:59,480 --> 01:13:02,649
(They were once a team, but their destinies diverged.)

1734
01:13:02,650 --> 01:13:05,019
(Good job.)

1735
01:13:05,020 --> 01:13:08,789
Still, I'm happy to have achieved this result...

1736
01:13:08,790 --> 01:13:10,489
thanks to the judges appreciating...

1737
01:13:10,490 --> 01:13:13,859
the performance.

1738
01:13:13,860 --> 01:13:18,969
But it feels a bit sad...

1739
01:13:18,970 --> 01:13:22,170
to lose the colleagues I enjoyed dancing and working with.

1740
01:13:24,970 --> 01:13:29,039
She described it as a transformation from an angel into a devil,

1741
01:13:29,040 --> 01:13:31,249
- but it didn't resonate with me.
- It didn't click.

1742
01:13:31,250 --> 01:13:33,780
I certainly understood the angel image,

1743
01:13:34,010 --> 01:13:37,789
but the way the transformation played out wasn't very convincing.

1744
01:13:37,790 --> 01:13:39,549
Instead of focusing on the performance itself,

1745
01:13:39,550 --> 01:13:41,759
the sense of anxiety and tension came through so strongly.

1746
01:13:41,760 --> 01:13:43,860
And it was actually a bit uncomfortable to watch.

1747
01:13:43,920 --> 01:13:46,489
You know, the missions I faced during the show...

1748
01:13:46,490 --> 01:13:48,960
actually involved the kind of work...

1749
01:13:49,300 --> 01:13:51,269
I've always dealt with.

1750
01:13:51,270 --> 01:13:52,929
But what made it different was...

1751
01:13:52,930 --> 01:13:55,699
having comrades by my side.

1752
01:13:55,700 --> 01:13:58,569
I learned a lot, relied on them,

1753
01:13:58,570 --> 01:14:03,339
and shared the challenges together.

1754
01:14:03,340 --> 01:14:05,410
I'm truly happy and grateful for that experience.

1755
01:14:06,650 --> 01:14:09,579
If viewers can at least come to understand...

1756
01:14:09,580 --> 01:14:11,019
what a director actually does...

1757
01:14:11,020 --> 01:14:13,749
I think concept is the most important.

1758
01:14:13,750 --> 01:14:16,690
And that it involves handling a wide range of elements...

1759
01:14:17,260 --> 01:14:19,830
beyond just choreography,

1760
01:14:20,160 --> 01:14:22,299
if people could understand that,

1761
01:14:22,300 --> 01:14:25,870
then I think I've made the right decision to make the appearance.

1762
01:14:26,430 --> 01:14:30,370
If asked, whether I want to be a good choreographer or director,

1763
01:14:31,140 --> 01:14:35,080
I'd choose being a good director. That feels right to me.

1764
01:14:35,410 --> 01:14:36,740
I feel that being a good director is...

1765
01:14:36,810 --> 01:14:40,179
a role defined by the recognition of...

1766
01:14:40,180 --> 01:14:42,580
the people who worked right alongside me in the field.

1767
01:14:42,820 --> 01:14:46,350
I hope that for my coworkers, I remain a fond memory...

1768
01:14:46,890 --> 01:14:48,760
and a positive influence,

1769
01:14:48,920 --> 01:14:51,430
and that I also leave a lasting impression on the audience.

1770
01:14:53,330 --> 01:14:56,300
I believe this reflects the qualities of a top director.

1771
01:14:57,200 --> 01:14:58,370
I've blossomed into a top director.

1772
01:14:59,770 --> 01:15:01,900
You've worked very hard. Keep up the great work.

1773
01:15:04,340 --> 01:15:06,239
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

1774
01:15:06,240 --> 01:15:07,909
(National Tour Concert Information)

1775
01:15:07,910 --> 01:15:09,009
Why are you crying?

1776
01:15:09,010 --> 01:15:11,080
You've done a good job. Keep it up.

1777
01:15:11,140 --> 01:15:13,280
- Simeez.
- BADA.

1778
01:15:14,010 --> 01:15:16,050
- What do I do from now on?
- No.

1779
01:15:16,150 --> 01:15:18,050
BADA, show them the power of women!

1780
01:15:18,220 --> 01:15:21,260
What are you saying? I can only do that if you are here.

1781
01:15:21,860 --> 01:15:27,860
(Eliminated choreographer, Simeez)

1782
01:15:30,060 --> 01:15:32,330
Street World Fighter: Directors' War...

1783
01:15:32,930 --> 01:15:33,969
(The highly anticipated semi-final mission)

1784
01:15:33,970 --> 01:15:36,170
It is the brand performance film mission.

1785
01:15:37,440 --> 01:15:39,039
- iPhone?
- It's the commercial, isn't it?

1786
01:15:39,040 --> 01:15:40,209
That is incredible.

1787
01:15:40,210 --> 01:15:41,809
Are we filming it ourselves?

1788
01:15:41,810 --> 01:15:43,110
This is really crazy.

1789
01:15:43,180 --> 01:15:44,509
You will serve as a director...

1790
01:15:44,510 --> 01:15:47,979
while also acting as an official model for a global smartphone brand.

1791
01:15:47,980 --> 01:15:49,049
(Incredible)

1792
01:15:49,050 --> 01:15:52,089
I really wanted to be in a smartphone commercial before.

1793
01:15:52,090 --> 01:15:53,249
That was my dream.

1794
01:15:53,250 --> 01:15:55,820
I really want to be chosen as the director.

1795
01:15:55,860 --> 01:15:56,919
(Gosh)

1796
01:15:56,920 --> 01:15:58,790
I've never wanted something so bad.

1797
01:15:59,290 --> 01:16:00,590
(I really wanted it.)

1798
01:16:00,690 --> 01:16:01,699
(This is awesome.)

1799
01:16:01,700 --> 01:16:03,799
This is something of great pride for me.

1800
01:16:03,800 --> 01:16:05,429
(I really have to do this.)

1801
01:16:05,430 --> 01:16:07,269
This is such a huge benefit, really.

1802
01:16:07,270 --> 01:16:09,369
Wouldn't you want to try shooting that commercial at least once?

1803
01:16:09,370 --> 01:16:10,799
(What a great scale, this is.)

1804
01:16:10,800 --> 01:16:12,539
Now, I truly have no regrets.

1805
01:16:12,540 --> 01:16:14,369
I truly have no regrets. But just this one thing.

1806
01:16:14,370 --> 01:16:15,379
(Model?)

1807
01:16:15,380 --> 01:16:16,810
(You have got to do it.)

1808
01:16:16,840 --> 01:16:21,049
(The five choreographers will each produce a solo performance film.)

1809
01:16:21,050 --> 01:16:22,349
(Three judges will select one Movement Director.)

1810
01:16:22,350 --> 01:16:25,649
We will select only one Movement Director.

1811
01:16:25,650 --> 01:16:28,119
I'm confident with my final result.

1812
01:16:28,120 --> 01:16:29,689
I really want the director's position.

1813
01:16:29,690 --> 01:16:30,889
(I really want to do it.)

1814
01:16:30,890 --> 01:16:32,259
I am so confident to do well.

1815
01:16:32,260 --> 01:16:33,429
(This is good.)

1816
01:16:33,430 --> 01:16:35,129
I can create the best result.

1817
01:16:35,130 --> 01:16:36,459
I have no concerns...

1818
01:16:36,460 --> 01:16:38,500
and I want to showcase my unique identity.

1819
01:16:39,000 --> 01:16:40,000
(I'm really confident.)

1820
01:16:40,001 --> 01:16:42,470
It looks like Kasper is trying out something different.

1821
01:16:42,700 --> 01:16:43,700
(It's not for me.)

1822
01:16:43,701 --> 01:16:46,370
There were movements that I do not prefer.

1823
01:16:46,540 --> 01:16:48,009
I thought that was really bad.

1824
01:16:48,010 --> 01:16:51,110
I don't know how I'm perceived by them, but...

1825
01:16:52,010 --> 01:16:53,049
(I want to break that.)

1826
01:16:53,050 --> 01:16:56,279
Are you thinking that everyone will do the arm movements together, too?

1827
01:16:56,280 --> 01:16:57,349
You know, that thing he always does.

1828
01:16:57,350 --> 01:16:58,889
(Flapping arms)

1829
01:16:58,890 --> 01:17:02,059
I don't think it would look cool if INGYOO and I did it.

1830
01:17:02,060 --> 01:17:05,429
I can already picture exactly what Koo Young is going to do.

1831
01:17:05,430 --> 01:17:07,329
Exploding from a single small energy...

1832
01:17:07,330 --> 01:17:09,000
and expanding into tremendous energy.

1833
01:17:09,500 --> 01:17:10,559
(I still don't quite understand it intuitively.)

1834
01:17:10,560 --> 01:17:11,799
(It's completely different...)

1835
01:17:11,800 --> 01:17:12,899
(from the vibe I had in mind.)

1836
01:17:12,900 --> 01:17:14,300
I becomes the energy itself.

1837
01:17:14,740 --> 01:17:15,740
(It's a bit old.)

1838
01:17:15,741 --> 01:17:17,869
It's like I ordered Iced Americano" but...

1839
01:17:17,870 --> 01:17:18,909
(Instead of coffee beans...)

1840
01:17:18,910 --> 01:17:20,239
(he put in beans for injeolmi.)

1841
01:17:20,240 --> 01:17:21,640
It's going to turn into roasted grain powder.

1842
01:17:22,040 --> 01:17:24,809
(Global smartphone brand model)

1843
01:17:24,810 --> 01:17:26,049
This is such a huge benefit.

1844
01:17:26,050 --> 01:17:27,549
I came back from the fire pit.

1845
01:17:27,550 --> 01:17:28,979
It's time for me to turn things over.

1846
01:17:28,980 --> 01:17:30,320
Only one gets...

1847
01:17:30,520 --> 01:17:32,589
(Last Stage: 24H Revealing one person to be saved)

1848
01:17:32,590 --> 01:17:34,859
(The three who aren't exempted...)

1849
01:17:34,860 --> 01:17:36,919
(will be confirmed for the Last Stage.)

1850
01:17:36,920 --> 01:17:40,489
I should be the one director...

1851
01:17:40,490 --> 01:17:42,629
who advances straight to the finals.

1852
01:17:42,630 --> 01:17:44,599
I think there's a good chance of winning...

1853
01:17:44,600 --> 01:17:45,699
(Goodness)

1854
01:17:45,700 --> 01:17:47,299
Koo Young has to go to the Last Stage.

1855
01:17:47,300 --> 01:17:48,839
It's about time he goes.

1856
01:17:48,840 --> 01:17:50,399
(He has to go, given public sentiment.)

1857
01:17:50,400 --> 01:17:51,770
I said to Koo Young...

1858
01:17:51,870 --> 01:17:52,969
(You should go to the Last Stage once.)

1859
01:17:52,970 --> 01:17:54,269
Anyone who's been to Last Stage...

1860
01:17:54,270 --> 01:17:56,279
would be absolutely green with envy with Koo Young...

1861
01:17:56,280 --> 01:17:57,540
(Won't let him go easily.)

1862
01:17:57,740 --> 01:17:59,549
I have no thoughts about the Last Stage.

1863
01:17:59,550 --> 01:18:00,609
(I won't be going.)

1864
01:18:00,610 --> 01:18:01,720
(Movement Director)

1865
01:18:01,880 --> 01:18:03,220
Where is he going?

1866
01:18:03,320 --> 01:18:04,719
Is that Koo Young's room?

1867
01:18:04,720 --> 01:18:05,950
He's going into Koo Young's room.

1868
01:18:06,390 --> 01:18:07,950
He's going to Koo Young.

1869
01:18:08,320 --> 01:18:09,359
(What do we do?)

1870
01:18:09,360 --> 01:18:11,089
Is Koo Young the only one that survives?

1871
01:18:11,090 --> 01:18:13,060
Gosh. I should prepare for the Last Stage quickly.

1872
01:18:13,560 --> 01:18:15,200
I'm going to the Last Stage.

1873
01:18:16,300 --> 01:18:18,299
I don't want to go to the Last Stage.

1874
01:18:18,300 --> 01:18:20,729
Result for the single finalist advancing to the finals.

1875
01:18:20,730 --> 01:18:23,100
Director Back Koo Young's next directing is...

1876
01:18:23,970 --> 01:18:25,670
(Last Directing Credit Board Director Back Koo Young)

1877
01:18:26,240 --> 01:18:28,139
The Final Survival Directing Battle...

1878
01:18:28,140 --> 01:18:30,240
"Last Stage: 24H."

1879
01:18:30,940 --> 01:18:33,279
Four years ago, during "Street Man Fighter,"

1880
01:18:33,280 --> 01:18:35,250
I was eliminated at this exact stage...

1881
01:18:36,880 --> 01:18:38,920
and failed to reach the finals.

1882
01:18:39,250 --> 01:18:41,020
Here and now, I will prove...

1883
01:18:41,860 --> 01:18:44,490
why I have survived this long.

1884
01:18:45,030 --> 01:18:46,490
I will prove myself.

1885
01:18:46,830 --> 01:18:49,500
The director who will claim the final spot in the finals...

1886
01:18:50,300 --> 01:18:52,300
In the end, I'm the one who's going to win.
